window.CMA_QS=[{"id":"v2-su20-q1278","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":1,"question":"1) All of the following are correct statements regarding the use of\ncloud computing for big data projects except","options":["Businesses are hesitant to invest in an extensive server and\nstorage infrastructure that might only be used occasionally to\ncomplete big data tasks.","Businesses only pay for the storage and computing time\nactually used.","An advantage of using cloud computing includes fast access to\nsoftware.","Analysts are not required to have a detailed understanding of\nthe available data and possess some sense of what answer(s)\nthey’re looking for.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Analysts must have a detailed understanding of the available\ndata and possess some sense of the answers they are looking\nfor. The value of data is only as valuable as the business\noutcomes it makes possible. It is how businesses make use of\ndata that allows full recognition of its true value and the\npotential to improve decision-making capabilities and measure\nthem against the results of positive business outcomes.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1279","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":2,"question":"2) The process of learning how the current system functions,\ndetermining the needs of users, and developing the logical\nrequirements of a proposed system is referred to as","options":["Systems maintenance.","Systems analysis.","Systems feasibility study.","Systems design."],"answer":"B","explanation":"A systems analysis requires a survey of the existing system,\nthe organization itself, and the organization’s environment to\ndetermine (among other things) whether a new system is\nneeded. The survey results determine not only what, where,\nhow, and by whom activities are performed but also why, how\nwell, and whether they should be done at all. Ascertaining the\nproblems and informational needs of decision makers is the\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\nnext step. The systems analyst must consider the entity’s key\nsuccess variables (factors that determine its success or\nfailure), the decisions currently being made and those that\nshould be made, the factors important in decision making\n(timing, relation to other decisions, etc.), the information\nneeded for decisions, and how well the current system makes\nthose decisions. Finally, the systems analysis should establish\nthe requirements of a system that will meet user needs.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1280","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":3,"question":"3) The least risky strategy for converting from a manual to a\ncomputerized accounts receivable system would be a","options":["Direct conversion.","Parallel conversion.","Pilot conversion.","Database conversion."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The least risky strategy for converting from a manual to a\ncomputerized system is a parallel conversion in which the old\nand new systems are operated simultaneously until\nsatisfaction is obtained that the new system is operating as\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\nexpected. Slightly more risky is a pilot conversion in which the\nnew system is introduced by module or segment.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1281","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":4,"question":"4) Which of the following are objectives for performing tests\nduring system development?\nI. System responds correctly to all kinds of inputs\nII. System achieves the general result its stakeholders\ndesire\nIII. System meets the requirements that guided its design\nand development\nIV. System performs its functions within an acceptable\ntime","options":["I and III only.","II, III, and IV only.","I, II, and IV only.","I, II, III, and IV."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Testing is performed during system development with the\nintent of identifying errors or other defects. The job of testing is\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\nan iterative process as when one error is corrected, it can\nilluminate other errors or even create new ones. All of the\nobjectives listed are objectives for performing tests during\nsystem development.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1282","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":5,"question":"5) Two phases of systems planning are project definition and\nproject initiation. All of the following are steps in the project\ninitiation phase except","options":["Preparing the project proposal.","Informing managers and employees of the project.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","Assembling the project team.","Training selected personnel."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The project initiation phase includes promptly informing\nmanagers and employees about the project, assembling the\nproject team (possibly including systems analysts,\nprogrammers, accountants, and users), training selected\npersonnel to improve necessary skills and enhance\ncommunication among team members, and establishing\nproject controls (e.g., by implementing a project scheduling\ntechnique such as PERT). Preparing the project proposal is a\npart of the project definition phase, as are conducting\nfeasibility studies, determining project priority, and submitting\nthe proposal for approval.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1283","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":6,"question":"6) An analyst prepared a forecast using newly developed system\nfeatures. The analyst recently left the company and her\nreplacement was unable to understand how to use these\nsystem functionalities. In accordance with systems\ndevelopment life-cycle best practices, which one of the\nfollowing controls would have prevented this situation from\noccurring?","options":["End-user computing efforts are outlined.","Documentation standards and procedures are developed.","Backup activities and requirements are put into place.","Changes made to the system are monitored and evaluated."],"answer":"B","explanation":"A requirement for documentation standards would have\nprevented the problem.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1284","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":7,"question":"7) Software-as-a-service can best be defined as a(n)","options":["On-premises ERP system installed and serviced locally.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","Type of cloud computing in which applications are hosted by a\nthird party for a monthly fee.","Type of database management system serviced by a third\nparty for an annual fee.","Infrastructure platform that replaces complex individual\ncomputers within a business."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Software-as-a-service (SaaS) is a software-user distribution\nmodel wherein a third-party provider hosts applications and\nmakes them available to subscribers over the Internet. With\nthis model, the user does not have to buy and maintain as\nmuch computer hardware, install software, or worry about\nmanning support services. Other benefits of SaaS include\nflexible payments, scalable usage, automatic updates, and\nflexible accessibility.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1285","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":8,"question":"8) An insurance firm that follows the systems development life\ncycle concept for all major information system projects is\npreparing to start a feasibility study for a proposed\nunderwriting system. Some of the primary factors the feasibility\nstudy should include are\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","options":["Possible vendors for the system and their reputation for\nquality.","Exposure to computer viruses and other intrusions.","Methods of implementation, such as parallel or cutover.","Technology and related costs."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The feasibility study should consider the activity to be\nautomated, the needs of the user, the type of equipment\nrequired, the cost, and the potential benefit to the specific area\nand the company in general. Thus, technical feasibility and\ncost are determined during this stage.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1286","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":9,"question":"9) The process of monitoring, evaluating, and modifying a system\nas needed is referred to as","options":["Systems analysis.","Systems feasibility study.","Systems maintenance.","Systems implementation."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Systems maintenance must be undertaken by systems\nanalysts and applications programmers continuously\nthroughout the life of a system. Maintenance is the redesign of\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\nthe system and programs to meet new needs or to correct\ndesign flaws. Ideally, these changes should be made as part\nof a regular program of preventive maintenance.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1287","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":10,"question":"10) Workwell Company operates in several regions, with each\nregion performing its data processing in a regional data center.\nThe corporate management information systems (MIS) staff\nhas developed a database management system to handle\ncustomer service and billing. The director of MIS\nrecommended that the new system be implemented in the\nSouthwestern Region to ascertain if the system operates in a\nsatisfactory manner. This type of conversion is called a","options":["Parallel conversion.","Direct conversion.","Prototype conversion.","Pilot conversion."],"answer":"D","explanation":"A modular conversion approach entails switching to the new\nor improved system in organizational (division, region, product\nline, etc.) segments or system segments (accounts receivable,\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\ndatabase, etc.). A pilot conversion is one in which the final\ntesting and switchover are accomplished at one segment or\ndivision of the company.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1288","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":11,"question":"11) An information system (IS) project manager is currently in the\nprocess of adding a systems analyst to the IS staff. The new\nsystems analyst will be involved with testing the new\ncomputerized system. At which stage of the systems\ndevelopment life cycle will the analyst be primarily used?","options":["Cost-benefit analysis.","Requirements definition.","Flowcharting.","Development."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The systems development life-cycle approach is the oldest\nmethodology applied to the development of medium or large\ninformation systems. The cycle is analytically divisible into\nstages: definition, design, development, implementation, and\nmaintenance. Testing is the most crucial step in the\ndevelopment stage of the life cycle.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1289","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":12,"question":"12) A major disadvantage of the life cycle approach to system\ndevelopment is that it is not well-suited for projects that are","options":["Structured.","Large.","Complex.","Unstructured."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The life cycle approach is best employed when systems are\nlarge and highly structured, users understand the tasks to be\nperformed by the information system, and the developers\nhave directly applicable experience in designing similar\nsystems. In the life cycle process, each stage of development\nis highly structured, and requirements are clearly defined.\nHowever, when the task is unstructured, prototyping may be\nthe better approach.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1290","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":13,"question":"13) Which of the following large-scale conversion approaches to\nsystem implementation presents the greatest risk to an\norganization?","options":["Parallel.","Direct.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","Phase-in.","Pilot."],"answer":"B","explanation":"With direct changeover (direct cutover) conversion, the old\nsystem is shut down and the new one takes over processing\nat once. This may be the least expensive and time-consuming\nstrategy, but it is the riskiest because the new system cannot\nbe reverted to the original.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1291","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":14,"question":"14) In which of the following phases of computer system\ndevelopment would training occur?","options":["Planning phase.","Analysis phase.","Design phase.","Implementation phase."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Training occurs during the implementation (installation and\noperation) phase of computer system development. Training\nand educating users is important not only for proper use of the\nsystem, but also to offset the resistance of users whose jobs\nmay have been substantially changed. This phase also\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\nincludes acceptance testing, system conversion, and system\nfollow-up.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1292","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":15,"question":"15) The process of developing specifications for hardware,\nsoftware, manpower, data resources, and information products\nrequired to develop a system is referred to as","options":["Systems analysis.","Systems feasibility study.","Systems maintenance.","Systems design."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Detailed systems design involves developing specifications\nregarding input, processing, internal controls and security\nmeasures, programs, procedures, output, and databases.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1293","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":16,"question":"16) Errors are most costly to correct during","options":["Programming.","Conceptual design.","Analysis.","Implementation.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Errors can be corrected most easily and clearly when they are\nfound at an early stage of systems development. Their\ncorrection becomes more costly as the life cycle progresses.\nBecause implementation is the last stage of the process listed,\nerrors are most costly to correct when discovered at the\nimplementation stage.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1294","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":17,"question":"17) Advantages of life cycle methodologies are","options":["Lower overall development costs when requirements change\nfrequently.","Ability to give users a functioning system quickly.","Reduced application development time to achieve a\nfunctioning system.","Enhanced management and control of the development\nprocess."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The systems development life cycle approach is the most\ncommon methodology applied to the development of large,\nhighly structured application systems. The life cycle approach\nis based on the idea that an information system has a finite life\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\nspan that is limited by the changing needs of the organization.\nThis cycle is analytically divisible into stages. A new system\nlife cycle begins when the inadequacy of the current system\nleads to a decision to develop a new or improved system. This\nmethod is a structured process for controlling the creative\nactivity required to devise, develop, and implement an\ninformation system. The process is described in varying terms\nby different writers, but the nature and sequence of the steps\nare essentially the same. Life cycle methodologies provide\nenhanced management and control of the development\nprocess because they provide structure for a creative process\nby dividing it into manageable steps and specifying what must\nbe produced in each phase.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1295","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":18,"question":"18) Which of the following is the final step before placing the\nsystem in live operation?","options":["Phased conversion.","User acceptance testing.","Dynamic testing.","Static testing."],"answer":"B","explanation":"IT must demonstrate to the user department that the system\nperforms the desired functionality. Once the user department\nis satisfied with the new system, they acknowledge formal\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\nacceptance and implementation begins. Thus, user\nacceptance testing is the final step before placing the system\nin live operation.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1296","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":19,"question":"19) Effective internal control for application development should\nprovide for which of the following?\nI. A project steering committee to initiate and oversee\nthe system\nII. A technical systems programmer to evaluate systems\nsoftware\nIII. Feasibility studies to evaluate existing systems\nIV. The establishment of standards for systems design\nand programming","options":["I and III only.","I, II, and IV only.","I, III, and IV only.","II, III, and IV only."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Effective systems development requires participation by top\nmanagement. This can be achieved through a steering\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\ncommittee composed of higher-level representatives of system\nusers. The committee approves or recommends projects and\nreviews their progress. Studies of the economic, operational,\nand technical feasibility of new applications necessarily entail\nevaluations of existing systems. Another necessary control is\nthe establishment of standards for system design and\nprogramming. Standards represent user and system\nrequirements determined during systems analysis.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1297","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":20,"question":"20) Which of the following best describes acceptance testing?","options":["Determines whether the system meets the organization’s\nneeds and is ready for release.","Tests a completely integrated system to verify that the system\nmeets its requirements.","Seeks to verify the interfaces between components against\nsoftware design.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","Verifies the functionality of a specific section of code and the\nhandling of data passed between various units."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Acceptance testing is conducted to determine whether the\nsystem meets the organization’s needs and is ready for\nrelease.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1298","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":21,"question":"21) Ordinarily, the analysis tool for the systems analyst and\nsteering committee to use in selecting the best system\nalternative is","options":["Pilot testing.","User selection.","Decision tree analysis.","Cost-benefit analysis."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Feasibility studies should include an analysis of the cost-\nbenefit ratio of any system alternatives. In many cases, the\nbest possible system may not be cost effective. Thus, once\nthe decision makers have determined that two or more\nsystems alternatives are acceptable, the cost-benefit analysis\nshould be used to select the best system for a particular\napplication.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1299","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":22,"question":"22) A systems development approach used to quickly produce a\nmodel of user interfaces, user interactions with the system,\nand process logic is called\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","options":["Neural networking.","Prototyping.","Reengineering.","Application generation."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Prototyping produces the first model(s) of a new system. This\ntechnique usually employs a software tool for quick\ndevelopment of a model of the user interface (such as by\nreport or screen), interaction of users with the system (for\nexample, a menu-screen approach or data entry), and\nprocessing logic (the executable module). Prototyping\nstimulates user participation because the model allows for\nquick exploration of concepts and development of solutions\nwith quick results.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1300","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":23,"question":"23) At what phase in the systems development process is a report\ngenerated that describes the content, processing flows,\nresource requirements, and procedures of a preliminary\nsystem design?","options":["File and database design.","Conceptual systems design.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","Physical systems design.","Procedures design."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The systems development life cycle begins with recognizing\nthat there is a need for a new system, gaining an\nunderstanding of the situation to determine whether it is\nfeasible to create a solution, and formulating a plan. A formal\nproposal for a new system is submitted to the IT steering\ncommittee, describing the need for the application and the\nbusiness function(s) that it will affect. Feasibility studies are\nconducted to determine (1) the technology the new system will\nrequire, (2) the economic resources that must be committed to\nthe new system, and (3) the impact the new system will have\non current operations.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1301","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":24,"question":"24) Which of the following is a correct statement regarding phased\nconversion?","options":["The old system is shut down, and the new one takes over\nprocessing immediately.","The old and new systems both run at full capacity for a given\nperiod.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","One function at a time of the new system is placed in\noperation.","One branch, department, or division at a time is fully converted\nto the new system."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Information technology conversion can involve hardware,\noperating systems, database management systems, and\napplications. Conversion methods utilized are (1) direct\ncutover, (2) pilot conversion, (3) phased conversion, and (4)\nparallel conversion. Under phased conversion, one function of\nthe new system at a time is placed in operation. For instance,\nif the new system is an integrated accounting application,\naccounts receivable could be installed, then accounts payable,\ncash management, materials handling, etc.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1302","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":25,"question":"25) All of the following are characteristics associated with direct\ncutover conversion except","options":["Time-saving.","Risky.","Inexpensive.","Safe.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Direct cutover conversion involves simultaneously shutting\ndown the old system and having the new one take over\nprocessing immediately. Direct cutover is the least expensive\nand time-consuming strategy, but it is also the riskiest.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1303","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":26,"question":"26) What should a company do when seeking competitive\nadvantages in planning for the implementation of a new\nsoftware system?","options":["Design an optimal process and then align the software.","Design the software to fit the existing processes.","Direct manpower to the nonbottleneck process areas.","Allow management to dictate processes.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation"],"answer":"A","explanation":"IT pervades every aspect of operations in a modern\norganization, and the IT steering committee must study each\nrequest for a new process and either approve or deny it. Once\na new process or system has been approved, a project team\nis assembled, consisting of representatives of the end users\nwho requested it and the IT personnel who will design and\nbuild the software components that will support it.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1304","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":27,"question":"27) Which of the following conversion strategies is characterized\nby a manager removing the old system and installing the new\nsystem without the possibility of reverting to the original?","options":["Direct changeover.","Phased implementation.","Parallel conversion.","Integrated test facility."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Under a direct changeover (direct cutover), the old system is\nshut down and the new one takes over processing\nimmediately, thereby removing the possibility of reverting to\nthe original.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1305","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":28,"question":"28) In an effort to recognize improvement opportunities, a\ncompany is reviewing its in-house systems. The best reason\nfor the company to consider switching to cloud computing as a\nsolution is that it","options":["Is the best way to secure sensitive corporate information.","Is accessible only from within the company on its intranet.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","Usually has lower upfront costs for equipment and\nmaintenance.","Provides better program modification options."],"answer":"C","explanation":"With cloud computing, organizations are relieved of the need\nto manage the storage of both application and data. It is\ntypically pay-per-use and self serviced. Hence, it usually has\nlower upfront costs for equipment and maintenance.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1306","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":29,"question":"29) Cloud computing can best be defined as a model that","options":["Streamlines business processes onto a well-secured and\nhighly available in-house e-commerce platform to optimize\ncustomers’ online experience.","Is designed for rapid application deployment by making\nseveral virtual servers run on one physical host.","Allows users to access network resources from remote\nlocations through a virtual private network.","Allows organizations to use the Internet to access and use\nservices and applications that run on remote third-party\ntechnology infrastructure.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Cloud computing can be used for management and storage of\nboth applications and data where all the software and data are\nstored via the Internet. It allows organizations to access\nservices and applications that run on remote third-party hosts.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1307","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":30,"question":"30) A company has abandoned the large array of dedicated\nservers it formerly used to store and provide access to its\ndatabase. The company has entered into a contract with a\nprovider who will guarantee storage of the database at its own\nlocation along with access over the Internet. This arrangement\nis an example of","options":["Distributed computing.","Cloud computing.","Wide area network.","Ethernet."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Cloud computing is a popular term relating to on-demand\naccess to resources that are accessed on the Internet and\nshared by others. The entity has the ability to choose and pay\nfor only the applications needed from the array (cloud) of\nresources, reducing the need for a large investment in IT\ninfrastructure.\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1308","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":31,"question":"31) A company is considering a move to a Software-as-a-Service\n(SaaS) offering instead of a traditional in-house application.\nWhich of the following concerns is unique to SaaS?","options":["Disaster recovery capabilities and documented recovery\nprocedures.","User credential setup and control over the actions that\nemployees can perform.","Allocation of software expenses and overhead charged to\ndepartments.","Ownership of processed data and costs of data migrations."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Software-as-a-Service is one of the three primary cloud\nservices. A concern for companies considering SaaS is\nownership of processed data because, compared to traditional\nin-house systems, cloud services are not as stringent in the\nmaintenance of ownership and are more susceptible to\nunauthorized access through hacking. Additionally, unlike a\n\n1: Technology-Enabled Finance Transformation\ntraditional in-house system, the use of cloud computing will\nlikely incur additional costs when data migrations occur.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\n20: (90) Systems Development and Data Analytics\n2: (59) Analytics and Big Data\nSubunit 2: Analytics and Big Data","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1309","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":1,"question":"1) A financial analyst is determining the probability that certain\ncustomers will default on their loans. Which one of the\nfollowing statistical models would be the best model to use to\nestimate this probability?","options":["Time series analysis.","Logistic regression.","Monte Carlo analysis.","Simple linear regression."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Logistic regression is a statistical model that estimates the\nprobability of an event occurring given a dataset of\nindependent variables. The binary dependent variable is\nbetween 0 and 1. An example is borrower will default on loan\nor borrower will pay back loan.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1310","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":2,"question":"2) Which one of the following statements is the best description\nof logistic regression?\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","options":["A statistical tool that estimates the linear relationship between\na dependent variable and one or more independent variables.","A statistical technique used to explore data and group the data\ninto predefined categories.","A predictive modeling method that differs from standard linear\nregression in that it uses binary valued outcomes.","A predictive technique that estimates future values based on a\nsequence of data points collected over time."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Logistic regression is a statistical model that estimates the\nprobability of an event occurring given a dataset of\nindependent variables. The binary dependent variable is\nbetween 0 and 1. Examples include the following: candidate\nwill pass or candidate will fail, borrower will default on loan or\nborrower will pay back loan, email is spam or email is not\nspam, and transaction is fraud or transaction is not fraud.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1311","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":3,"question":"3) The data analytics tool that is used to explore data sets and\ngroup them into predefined categories is called","options":["Classification.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","Clustering.","Linear regression.","Logistic regression."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Classification is a statistical technique used to explore data\nand group the data into predefined categories.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1312","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":4,"question":"4) All of the following are correct statements regarding big\ndata except","options":["Big data is an evolving term that describes any voluminous\namount of structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data\nthat has the potential to be mined for information.","Big data includes information collected from social media, data\nfrom Internet-enabled devices, machine data, video, and voice\nrecordings. The information collected is converted from high-\ndensity data into low-density data.","Big data is often characterized by the “4 Vs”: volume, variety,\nvelocity, and veracity.","Big data involves processing data with analytic and algorithmic\ntools to reveal meaningful information."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The information collected is converted from low-density data\nto high-density data, not from high-density data to low-density\ndata.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1313","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":5,"question":"5) A hospital has observed an increase in the number of cases of\na disease and has asked an analyst to collect data on the\ncases over the last 3 years. The analyst noted that the disease\nappeared 3 years ago during the second quarter of the year.\nSince then, the third and fourth quarters of each year showed\nsignificant spikes in the number of cases when compared to\nthe first two quarters. What is the best way to present these\nfindings?","options":["Table, showing the number of cases in each month for the last\n3 years.","Pie chart, showing the number of cases in each quarter for the\nlast 3 years.","Scatter plot, showing the change in the number of cases for\neach quarter for the last 3 years.","Bar graph, showing the number of cases in each quarter for\nthe last 3 years.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data"],"answer":"D","explanation":"A bar chart (also called bar graph) is the best way to present\nthe findings because it shows the number of cases each\nquarter in comparison to other quarters.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1314","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":6,"question":"6) Which one of the following statements defines data mining?","options":["A process of using statistical techniques to extract and analyze\ndata from large databases to discern patterns and trends.","A system used to develop a firm’s performance metrics.","A process of using algorithms that serve to facilitate efficient\ncommunication within a firm.","A system used to organize and interpret complex data to\nensure the data has been accurately recorded in the database.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Data mining examines large amounts of data to discover\npatterns using statistical models and techniques. The term\ndata mining is somewhat misleading because its purpose is\nthe discovery of patterns in large amounts of data, not the\nextraction of the data itself.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1315","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":7,"question":"7) A simple regression equation has an r 2 of 0.85. This means\nthat","options":["85% of the variation of the dependent variable is explained by\nthe regression line.","85% of the variation of the independent variable is explained\nby the regression line.","The dependent and independent variables have a correlation\ncoefficient of 0.85.","The dependent variable does not have a strong correlation\nwith the independent variable.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The coefficient of determination (r 2) is a measure of the fit\nbetween the independent and dependent variables. The\ncoefficient of determination is the proportion of the total\nvariation in the dependent variable that is accounted for by the\nindependent variable. The value of r 2 ranges from 0 to 1. The\ncloser the value of r 2 to 1, the more useful the independent\nvariable (x) is for explaining or predicting the variation in the\ndependent variable (y). A coefficient of determination of 0.85\nequals 85% of the variation of the dependent variable\nexplained by the regression line.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1316","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":8,"question":"8) The type of data analytics that is most likely to yield the most\nimpact for an organization but is also the most complex is\ncalled","options":["Diagnostic analysis.","Predictive analysis.","Descriptive analysis.","Prescriptive analysis."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Prescriptive analysis concentrates on what an organization\nneeds to do in order for the predicted future results to actually\noccur. In other words, prescriptive analysis tells a company\nhow to get to where it wants to go. This type of analysis\nprovides the most benefit but requires more inputs.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1317","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":9,"question":"9) An organization wants to utilize business intelligence (BI) to\nassist in the evaluation of key metrics. The IT manager has\nsuggested incorporating a dashboard feature in its BI tool.\nWhich one of the following is the main reason that\nmanagement should implement the dashboard feature?","options":["It allows management to have as many different charts as\npossible.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","It shows patterns and trends in data across the organization.","It is designed to focus on metrics that have not been met.","It can automatically generate reorders of important materials\nfor production."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Business intelligence refers to software applications, tools,\nand practices that can be used to analyze and organize raw\ndata. The objective is to speed up and improve managerial\ndecision making and to uncover new business opportunities.\nVisualizing and analyzing business data can be easier with\ndashboard features. A standard dashboard for key analytical\nfunctions makes collaboration easier by enabling a large\norganization to share its analyses across the entire entity.\nBasically, a dashboard is defined as an interactive user\ninterface that presents information in an easy-to-read and\neasy-to-understand manner.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1318","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":10,"question":"10) A car insurance company is considering opening branches in a\nforeign country. The country’s population has been growing\nrapidly for the last 5 years. The company wants to know\nwhether the number of car accidents are correlated with the\nrecent population growth. Which of the following charts\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nprepared by an analyst would be most helpful to the\ncompany?","options":["A line chart showing each month on the x-axis and the number\nof car accidents on the y-axis.","A scatter plot showing the number of car accidents on the y-\naxis and the population size on the x-axis.","A table showing the number of car accidents in rows and the\npopulation size in columns.","A pie chart showing the number of car accidents in each city\nfor the last 5 years."],"answer":"B","explanation":"A scatter plot is the best way to present the relationship by\nillustrating the correlation between the number of car\naccidents (y variable) and the population size (x variable).","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1319","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":11,"question":"11) Which of the following is included in the Four Vs of big data?","options":["Volume.","Velocity.","Variety.","All of the answers are correct.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The four Vs of big data include volume, velocity, variety, and\nveracity. Some people include the value of the data as a fifth\nV.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1320","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":12,"question":"12) In a regression analysis, the coefficient of determination (r 2)","options":["Identifies the causal factor in a linear model.","Tests that the independent variable has no correlation with the\ndependent variable.","Assesses how well a model can predict an outcome.","Is the proportion of the variance in the independent variable\nthat is predictable from the dependent variable.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The coefficient of determination (r 2) is a measure of the fit\nbetween the independent and dependent variables. The\ncoefficient of determination is the proportion of the total\nvariation in the dependent variable that is accounted for by the\nindependent variable. The value of r 2 ranges from 0 to 1. The\ncloser the value of r 2 to 1, the more useful the independent\nvariable (x) is for explaining or predicting the variation in the\ndependent variable (y).","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1321","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":13,"question":"13) A company developed the following multiple regression\nequation, utilizing 10 years of data, and uses it to estimate the\ncost of its product.\nTotal cost = F + aL + bM\nWhere: F = fixed costs\nL = labor rate per hour\nM = material cost per pound\nWhich of the following changes would most likely have the\ngreatest impact on invalidating the results of this model?","options":["Changing the source of material to a low-cost foreign source.","A significant reduction in factory overhead.","A significant change in labor productivity.","Renegotiation of the union contract resulting in a higher wage\nrate."],"answer":"C","explanation":"A change in labor productivity would invalidate the results of\nthe model because the level of change is not known.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1322","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":14,"question":"14) Business intelligence (BI) has all of the following\ncharacteristics except\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","options":["Focusing on strategic objectives.","Giving immediate information about an organization’s critical\nsuccess factors.","Displaying information in graphical format.","Providing advice and answers to top management from a\nknowledge-based system."],"answer":"D","explanation":"BI serves the needs of top management for managerial control\nand strategic planning. BI focuses on strategic (long-range)\nobjectives and gives immediate information about a firm’s\ncritical success factors. BI is not a program for providing top\nmanagement with advice and answers from a knowledge-\nbased (expert) system.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1323","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":15,"question":"15) Box Co. uses regression analysis to estimate the functional\nrelationship between an independent variable (cost driver) and\noverhead cost. Assume that the following equation is being\nused:\ny = a + bx\nWhat is the symbol for the independent variable?","options":["y.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","x.","bx.","a."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The simple regression equation is y = a + bx. The symbol y is\nthe dependent variable (overhead costs), a is the y-axis\nintercept (fixed costs), b is the slope of the regression line\n(cost driver), and x is the independent variable.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1324","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":16,"question":"16) A regression equation","options":["Estimates the dependent variable(s).","Encompasses factors outside the relevant range.","Is based on objective and constraint functions.","Estimates the independent variable.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Regression analysis is used to find an equation for the linear\nrelationship among variables. The behavior of the dependent\nvariable is explained in terms of one or more independent\nvariables. Regression analysis often is used to estimate a\ndependent variable (such as cost) given a known independent\nvariable (such as production).","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1325","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":17,"question":"17) Multiple regression differs from simple regression in that it","options":["Provides an estimated constant term.","Has more dependent variables.","Allows the computation of the coefficient of determination.","Has more independent variables."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Improved accuracy of forecasts may often be achieved by\nregressing the dependent variable on more than one\nindependent variable. The usual multiple regression equation\nis linear and is in the following form when y is the dependent\nvariable; a is the y-axis intercept; x1, x2, etc., are the\nindependent variables; b1, b2, etc., are the coefficients of the\nindependent variables; and e is the error term:\ny = a + b1x1 + b2x2 + ... + e","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1326","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":18,"question":"18) Multiple regression analysis involves the use of\nDependent Variables Independent Variables","options":["One More than one\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","More than one More than one","More than one One","One One"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Improved accuracy of forecasts may often be achieved by\nregressing the dependent variable on more than one\nindependent variable. The usual multiple regression equation\nis linear and is in the following form:\ny = a + bx1 + bx2 + ... + e","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1327","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":19,"question":"19) For cost estimation, simple regression differs from multiple\nregression in that simple regression uses only","options":["One dependent variable, while multiple regression uses all\navailable data to estimate the cost function.","Dependent variables, while multiple regression can use both\ndependent and independent variables.","One independent variable, while multiple regression uses\nmore than one independent variable.","One dependent variable, while multiple regression uses more\nthan one dependent variable."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Simple regression uses the algebraic formula for a straight\nline, y = a + bx, where x is the independent variable. Multiple\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nregression is used when there is more than one independent\nvariable. Multiple regression allows a firm to identify many\nfactors (independent variables) and to weight each one\naccording to its influences on the overall outcome (y = a +\nb1x1 + b2x2 + b3x3 + etc.).","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1328","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":20,"question":"20) In preparing the annual profit plan for the coming year, Fine\nCompany wants to determine the cost behavior pattern of the\nmaintenance costs. Fine has decided to use linear regression\nby employing the equation y = a + bx for maintenance costs.\nThe results of the regression analysis are given below.\na 684.65\nb 7.2884\nBased upon the data derived from the regression analysis,\n420 maintenance hours in a month would mean that Fine Co.’s\nmaintenance costs (rounded to the nearest dollar) would be\nbudgeted at","options":["$3,780","$3,600","$3,790\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","$3,746"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Substituting the given data into the regression equation results\nin a budgeted cost of $3,746 (rounded to the nearest dollar).\ny = a + bx\ny = 684.65 + 7.2884(420)\ny = $3,746","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1329","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":21,"question":"21) The letter x in the standard regression equation\nis best described as a(n)","options":["Independent variable.","Dependent variable.","Constant coefficient.","Coefficient of determination.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The letter x in the standard regression equation is the\nindependent variable. For example, in a regression to\ndetermine the total cost of production, x equals units\nproduced.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1330","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":22,"question":"22) In the standard regression equation y = a + bx, the letter b\nis best described as a(n)","options":["Independent variable.","Dependent variable.","Y intercept.","Slope of the regression line."],"answer":"D","explanation":"In the standard regression equation, b represents the slope of\nthe regression line. For example, in a cost determination\nregression, y equals total costs, b is the variable cost per unit,\nx is the number of units produced, and a is fixed cost.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1331","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":23,"question":"23) Which of the following best describes unstructured data?","options":["Data with a high level of organization.","Data systematically stored with markers to enforce hierarchies\nof records and fields within the data.","Information that is not organized in a pre-defined manner (e.g.,\ntext-heavy facts, dates, numbers, and images).","Conforms with the organization of data models associated with\nrelational databases."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Unstructured data refers to information that is not organized in\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\na pre-defined manner (e.g., text-heavy facts, dates, numbers,\nand images).","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1332","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":24,"question":"24) Each of the following represents a characteristic of big\ndata except","options":["Size.","Mixture.","Speed.","Uniformity."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Big data is often characterized by the “4 Vs” - volume, variety,\nvelocity, and veracity. Thus, uniformity is not a characteristic of\nbig data.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1333","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":25,"question":"25) Which of the following is a correct statement regarding\nvolume-based value?","options":["The faster businesses can inject data into their data and\nanalytics platform, the more time they will have to ask the right\nquestions and seek answers.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","Rapid analysis capabilities provide businesses with the right\ndecision in time to achieve their customer relationship\nmanagement objectives.","The more data businesses have on the customers, both recent\nand historical, the greater the insights.","In the digital era, capability to acquire and analyze varied data\nis extremely valuable."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The more data businesses have on the customers, both\nrecent and historical, the greater the insights is a correct\nstatement regarding volume-based value.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1334","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":27,"question":"27) An automobile parts manufacturer has received complaints\nfrom customers about declining quality. After a quick review,\nmanagement realizes the problem has no single source. To\nperform a thorough process of problem identification, the most\nappropriate tool is a(n)","options":["Fishbone diagram.","Histogram.","Pareto diagram.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","Statistical control charts."],"answer":"A","explanation":"A fishbone diagram (also called a cause-and-effect diagram or\nan Ishikawa diagram) is used in total quality management for\nprocess improvement. It is useful in studying causation (why\nthe actual and desired situations differ). This format organizes\nthe analysis of causation and helps to identify possible\ninteractions among causes.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1335","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":28,"question":"28) The new purchasing director is analyzing purchase orders for\nthe organization. Which of the following analyses\nwould best be displayed on a histogram?","options":["In the past year the organization placed 10,000 purchase\norders. Organize the number of orders placed with each\nsupplier, sorted in descending order.","The average turnaround time from issuing a purchase order to\nreceiving the merchandise is 7 days. Review the last 2,000\npurchase orders, and using 10 days as the upper control limit\nand 4 days as the lower control limit, graph the turnaround\ntime for each order.","The organization purchased US $27 million worth of inventory\nin the past year. Distribute by value, using US $500\nincrements, the quantity of purchase orders that fall within\neach range.","Identify and organize the reasons the average turnaround time\nfor purchase orders falls outside the control parameters of 4-\n10 days."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The histogram displays a continuous frequency distribution of\nthe independent variable in the form of a bar graph. The y axis\nis the quantity of purchase orders and the x axis is the\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\npurchase order amount. The histogram would best display the\nquantity of purchase orders by dollar value.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1336","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":29,"question":"29) The director of sales asks for a count of customers grouped in\ndescending numerical rank by (1) the number of orders they\nplace during a single year and (2) the dollar amounts of the\naverage order. The visual format of these two pieces of\ninformation is most likely to be a","options":["Fishbone diagram.","Cost of quality report.","Kaizen diagram.","Pareto diagram."],"answer":"D","explanation":"A Pareto diagram displays the values of an independent\nvariable such that managers can quickly identify the areas\nmost in need of attention. The variables involved must be\nquantifiable.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1337","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":30,"question":"30) A health insurer uses a computer application to monitor\nphysician bill amounts for various surgical procedures. This\nprogram allows the organization to better control\nreimbursement rates. The X-bar chart below is an example of\nthe output from this application.\nSelect the interpretation that best explains the data plotted on\nthe chart.","options":["Positive correlation.","Abnormal variation.","Normal variation.","Cyclic variation."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Statistical quality control charts are graphic aids for monitoring\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nthe status of any process subject to random variations. The X-\nbar chart presented here depicts the sample means for a\nvariable. If the values fall within the upper and lower control\nlimits, no action is taken. Accordingly, values outside these\nlimits are abnormal and should be investigated for possible\ncorrective action.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1338","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":31,"question":"31) Statistical quality control often involves the use of control\ncharts whose basic purpose is to","options":["Determine when accounting control procedures are not\nworking.","Control labor costs in production operations.","Detect performance trends away from normal operations.","Monitor internal control applications of information technology."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Statistical control charts are graphic aids for monitoring the\nstatus of any process subject to acceptable and unacceptable\nvariations during repeated operations. The chart consists of\nthree horizontal lines plotted on a horizontal time scale. The\nvertical scale represents the appropriate quantitative measure.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nThe center line represents the average range or overall mean\nfor the process being controlled. The other two lines are the\nupper control limit and the lower control limit. The processes\nare measured periodically, and the values are plotted on the\nchart. If the value falls within the control limits, no action is\ntaken. If the value falls outside the limits, the process is\nconsidered out of control, and an investigation is made for\npossible corrective action. Another advantage of the chart is\nthat it makes trends visible.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1339","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":32,"question":"32) A manufacturer mass produces nuts and bolts on its assembly\nline. The line supervisors sample every nth unit for\nconformance with specifications. Once a nonconforming part is\ndetected, the machinery is shut down and adjusted.\nThe most appropriate tool for this process is a","options":["Fishbone diagram.","Cost of quality report.","Regression analysis.","Statistical quality control chart.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Statistical quality control is a method of determining whether\nthe shipment or production run of units lies within acceptable\nlimits. It is also used to determine whether production\nprocesses are out of control. Statistical control charts are\ngraphic aids for monitoring the status of any process subject\nto random variations.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1340","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":33,"question":"33) A cost-volume-profit model developed in a dynamic\nenvironment determined that the estimated parameters used\nmay vary between limits. Subsequent testing of the model with\nrespect to all possible values of the estimated parameters is\ntermed","options":["A sensitivity analysis.","Learning curve analysis.","Expected value analysis.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","A time-series study."],"answer":"A","explanation":"After a problem has been formulated into any mathematical\nmodel, it may be subjected to sensitivity analysis. Sensitivity\nanalysis examines how the model’s outcomes change as the\nparameters change.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1341","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":34,"question":"34) A cereal producer often receives complaints that boxes are\nunderweight. To gather data on the extent of this problem, the\nproducer should develop which of the following?","options":["Fishbone diagram.","Statistical control chart.","Cost-of-quality analysis.","Pareto chart."],"answer":"B","explanation":"A statistical control chart is used to monitor the extent of\nvariances between actual and expected results. The chart has\nthree horizontal lines. The midline is the target value, and the\nother lines are the upper and lower control limits. Results are\nplotted on the chart. Accordingly, the cereal producer should\ndevelop a control chart to gather data on the extent of the\nvariances between the actual and expected (midline) weight(s)\nof the cereal boxes.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1342","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":35,"question":"35) Which of the following can be discovered using a data-mining\nprocess?\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","options":["Data structure.","Previously unknown information.","Artificial intelligence.","Standard query reporting."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Data mining examines large amounts of data to discover\npatterns in the data (i.e., unexpected relationships among\ndata). A classic example of the use of data mining is the\ndiscovery by convenience stores that diapers and beer often\nappear on the same sales transaction in the late evening.\nThus, previously unknown information can be discovered\nusing a data-mining process.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1343","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":36,"question":"36) Which of the following is a critical success factor in data mining\na large data store?","options":["Pattern recognition.","Effective search engines.","Image processing systems.","Accurate universal resource locator (URL)."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Data mining allows a user to discover hidden relationships,\nsuch as associations, sequences of events, classifications\n(descriptions of the groups to which the item belongs), or\nclusters (new groupings previously not known). Typical\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\napplications of data mining are identification of potential\ncustomers and purchasing power.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1344","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":37,"question":"37) Which of the following best describes a characteristic of big\ndata?","options":["Collected data often provides straightforward answers to\nusers.","Data collected are free from useless information or incorrect\nvariables.","Big data is in a visual context, such as a graph or chart, rather\nthan a text format.","Data of untapped markets is often not collected."],"answer":"D","explanation":"One limitation of big data is that user-level data results are\nincomplete. Generally, the data available to an organization\nare restricted to data of persons who have had some contact\nwith the organization (e.g., visited the organization’s website\nor called the organization). The data are only representative of\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nthe target market; thus, untapped markets could potentially\nexist, the data of which are not being captured.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1345","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":38,"question":"38) A company uses big data analytics in marketing. Which of the\nfollowing is a limitation of using big data?","options":["The company can use big data to predict customer behaviors.","Data results cannot be visualized to identify and forecast\ncustomer trends.","Big data cannot explain why customers behave in certain\nways.","Data collected only represent untapped customers but not\ntapped customers."],"answer":"C","explanation":"One limitation of big data is that determining why the analysis\nresults are what they are is difficult. While big data analysis\ncan show that there is a certain pattern in monthly sales, it\nfails to show what causes the pattern. Further and more\ncomplicated analyses are needed, the results of which tend to\nbe more difficult for non-technical people to understand.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1346","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":39,"question":"39) Data visualization\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","options":["Includes visualization tools such as bubble charts, pareto\ndiagrams, boxplots, and what-if analyses.","Ensures the presentation of trends and correlations are\nunderstood by a wider audience without bias.","Assists with big data analytics to display data results in a\nvisual context.","Is most useful to an audience when visualization tools present\nvarious items in different scales and skip values to highlight\nitems emphasized by the presenter."],"answer":"C","explanation":"One limitation of big data is that user-level data results require\ninterpretation prior to use. Data visualizations assist big data\nin identifying trends and correlations that run the risk of going\nundetected in text-based data.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1347","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":40,"question":"40) Which of the following is a best practice for visualization tools\nto avoid distortion in the communication of complex\ninformation?","options":["Exclude calculations from the design to ensure the user can\ninterpret data in their own way.","Present various items in different scales and skip values to\nhighlight items emphasized by the presenter.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","Use variant shades of the same color to present subgroups\nclassified under one group.","Ask others for feedback before finalizing the design to ensure\nunderstandability."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The presenter can ask others for feedback on the design\nbefore finalizing the presentation. Asking others for opinions\non whether too much information causes confusion or whether\nthe presentation is understandable are good approaches.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1348","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":41,"question":"41) Corporation B recently hired a financial analyst to improve its\nfinancial results. The analyst is interested in implementing a\nnew type of project analysis that will help evaluate the effects\nof small changes in advertising expenses on sales. The\nanalyst believes that this form of analysis will be useful in\nforecasting the impacts of resource allocation decisions. What\ntype of analysis is the analyst attempting to implement?","options":["Delphi approach.","What-if analysis.","The goodness-of-fit test.","Fishbone diagrams."],"answer":"B","explanation":"What-if analysis is a process of determining the effects on\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\noutcomes in a model through changes in scenarios. The\nanalyst is performing a what-if analysis by evaluating the\neffects of small changes in advertising expenses on sales to\nobtain better forecasts.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1349","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":42,"question":"42) Which of the following is a primary advantage of a what-if\nanalysis?","options":["It allows users to determine the effects of outcomes in all\nscenarios.","It summarizes opinions from many experts and feeds the\nsummaries back to the experts without revealing participants\nto each other.","It enables users to evaluate their outcomes by applying a goal\nseeking approach.","It results in a reduction of data and strengthened data integrity."],"answer":"C","explanation":"What-if analysis is a process of determining the effects on\noutcomes in a model through changes in scenarios. Goal\nseeking occurs when the decision maker has a specific\noutcome in mind and needs to determine how it can be\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nachieved. Thus, a what-if analysis enables users to evaluate\ntheir outcomes by applying a goal seeking approach.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1350","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":43,"question":"43) A cost accountant is updating its fourth quarter budget. The\nannual goal of cost savings is $56,000. The cost savings for\nthe first, second, and third quarters are $12,000, $6,700, and\n$9,200. The accountant performed an analysis to determine\nthe cost savings required for the fourth quarter to achieve the\nannual goal. This is an example of","options":["Monte Carlo simulation.","What-if analysis.","Predictive analytics.","Time series analysis."],"answer":"B","explanation":"What-if analysis is a process of determining the effects on\noutcomes in a model through changes in scenarios. Goal\nseeking occurs when the decision maker has a specific\noutcome in mind and needs to determine how it can be\nachieved. The accountant performs the analysis to determine\nfourth quarter cost savings so that the annual goal of $56,000\ncost savings will be achieved. This is an example of what-if\nanalysis.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1351","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":44,"question":"44) What-if analysis is also known as","options":["Goal seeking analysis.","Trend analysis.","Regression analysis.","Horizontal analysis."],"answer":"A","explanation":"What-if analysis is a process of determining the effects on\noutcomes in a model through changes in scenarios. What-if\nanalysis is also known as goal seeking analysis. Goal seeking\noccurs when the decision maker has a specific outcome in\nmind and needs to determine how it can be achieved.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1352","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":45,"question":"45) Which of the following best represents the application of\npredictive analytics?","options":["The human resource manager prepares an analysis to show\nwhich departments have the highest employee turnover.","The website recommends pet toys and bedding after the\ncustomer purchases pet food.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","A consultant organizes an analysis of causation for dissatisfied\nworkers and possible interactions among causes.","A cost accountant monitors whether direct materials used are\nwithin the acceptable variations for the last 6 months."],"answer":"B","explanation":"A common use of predictive analytics in the retail sector\noccurs when a customer selects an item to purchase online\nand prepares to finalize the transaction; the web page then\ndisplays additional products other customers purchased in\nconjunction with the initial item.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1353","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":46,"question":"46) Which of the following techniques are most effective in\nidentifying trends and patterns?","options":["Time series analysis, exploratory data analysis, predictive\nanalytics.","Fishbone diagrams, time series analysis, predictive analytics.","Exploratory data analysis, Pareto diagrams, scatter plots.","Line charts, scatter plots, Delphi approach."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Time series analysis is the process of projecting future trends\nbased on past experiences. Exploratory data analysis is an\napproach to data analysis that seeks to open-mindedly\nobserve the data in order to gain some new, often\nunexpected, insight into the data. Predictive analytics uses\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\ndata, statistical algorithms, and machine learning techniques\nto draw insights on such trends as consumer or industry\nbehavior patterns. All three of these techniques are effective in\nidentifying trends and patterns.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1354","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":47,"question":"47) Exploratory data analysis","options":["Rarely uses graphical tools in order to avoid bias generated\nfrom manipulating visualization tools.","Aims to reveal patterns and discover insights by uncovering\nthe underlying structure of data.","Is often used as the last step of the data analysis process to\ngain new insight into the data.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","Often develops assumptions at an early stage so that\nanomalies can be identified sooner than traditional techniques."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Exploratory data analysis seeks to maximize insight into a\ndata set, uncover an underlying structure, and check for\noutliers and anomalies. The main role of exploratory data\nanalysis is to open-mindedly explore in order to gain some\nnew, often unexpected, insight into the data.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1355","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":48,"question":"48) A consultant is analyzing Company A’s sales report on pants.\nThe consultant has found that there are several unique\npatterns in the data. He noticed that there is a set of customers\nwho purchased mainly one to two different types of pants in a\nyear. This customer segment is the largest and is constantly\ngrowing. After further analyses he found that the pants\npurchased by each of these customers have different sizes.\nMore analyses revealed that these customers are small\nclothing retail stores. The consultant then started to analyze\nhow the company can improve supply chain management and\nbusiness relationships with this specific customer segment to\nimprove profitability. The method used in analyzing the\nproblem is best described as a(n)","options":["Monte Carlo simulation.","Regression analysis.","Sensitivity analysis.","Exploratory data analysis."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Exploratory data analysis is an approach to data analysis that\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\ndiffers from traditional modeling and analytic techniques by\nencouraging the data itself to reveal its underlying structure\nrather than prematurely applying a hypothesis or statistical\nmethod. It seeks to maximize insight into a data set, uncover\nan underlying structure, identify important variables, check for\noutliers and anomalies, test underlying assumptions, develop\nparsimonious models, and determine optimal factors. This is\nan example of exploratory data analysis.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1356","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":49,"question":"49) An analyst is preparing a time series analysis for the sales of\nswimwear. He notices that, for the last 3 years, the swimwear\nsales rise during May and August and fall during November\nand February. Which of the following patterns best describes\nthis scenario?","options":["Irregular pattern.","Cyclical pattern.","Chronological pattern.","Seasonal pattern."],"answer":"D","explanation":"A seasonal pattern often exists when a time series is\ninfluenced by seasonal factors (e.g., the quarter of the year,\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nthe month, or the day of the week). The swimwear sales rise\nduring May and August (summer months) and fall during\nNovember and February (winter months). Thus, this scenario\nis best described as a seasonal pattern.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1357","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":50,"question":"50) Which of the following most likely shows a cyclical pattern?","options":["Traffic peaks in the morning and evening hours.","An increase in sales of gloves in the winter.","Economic data affected by recession.","An increase in oil prices due to an oil workers’ strike."],"answer":"C","explanation":"A cyclical pattern exists when data points show rises and falls\nthat are not of a fixed or seasonal pattern. The duration of\nthese cyclical fluctuations is usually at least a couple of years.\nAn example is business cycles (i.e., expansion, peak,\nrecession, depression), which typically last several years, but\nthe length of the current cycle is never known in advance.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1358","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":51,"question":"51) Which of the following most likely shows an irregular pattern?","options":["Increase in GDP during expansion.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","Decrease in the number of tourists due to an earthquake.","Decrease in the sales of ice cream during winter.","Increase in the number of tourists during weekends and\nholidays."],"answer":"B","explanation":"An irregular pattern exists when random or unplanned factors\noccur. An earthquake is an unplanned factor. Thus, a\ndecrease in the number of tourists due to an earthquake is an\nexample of an irregular pattern.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1359","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":52,"question":"52) Time series analysis","options":["Uses trial and error to determine the effects of changes in\nassumptions on outcome.","Analyzes current results against past activity to determine\nshifts in trends.","Solicits opinions from experts, summarizes the opinions, and\nfeeds the summaries back to the experts without revealing\nparticipants to each other.","Assists with determining whether a sample is representative of\nthe population."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Time series analysis is the process of projecting future trends\nbased on past experience. Benefits of time series analysis\ninclude analyzing current results against activity in the past to\ndetermine trend shifts.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1360","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":53,"question":"53) Which is the correct order of the steps in the data mining\nprocess?\nI. Perform regression analysis to generate an equation\nthat models the data.\nII. Identify anomalies and unusual data records.\nIII. Prepare visual presentations and reports.\nIV. Generalize the relationships among data.\nV. Find relationships between variables and group the\nrelationships.","options":["I, V, IV, II, III.","II, V, IV, I, III.","II, I, IV, V, III.","II, IV, V, III, I."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The steps for the data mining process are\n1. Identify anomalies and unusual data records.\n2. Find relationships between variables and group the\nrelationships.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\n3. Generalize the relationships among data.\n4. Perform regression analysis to generate an equation\nthat models the data.\n5. Prepare visual presentations and reports.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1361","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":54,"question":"54) The goal of structured query language (SQL) is to","options":["Evaluate and document the structure of the database.","Clean up incorrect, incomplete, or duplicated data before\nuploading it into the database.","Create, update, retrieve, and manage data within a database.","Provide detailed information about the size, format, usage,\nmeaning, and ownership of every data element.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data"],"answer":"C","explanation":"SQL is a language used to access and manipulate data within\nrelational database management systems. Queries are\nconstructed and executed using a set of commands to create,\nupdate, and retrieve information.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1362","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":55,"question":"55) An analyst is performing a sensitivity analysis on how changes\nin the inflation rate and the interest rate can affect bond prices.\nWhich of the following most likely causes the sensitivity\nanalysis to be inaccurate?","options":["The interest rate changes affect bond prices to a greater\nextent than the inflation rate.","Inflation is expected to increase in the next year.","Bond prices are extremely volatile to both changes in inflation\nand interest rates.","Interest rates are affected by changes in the inflation rate."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Sensitivity analysis is limited due to the consideration of\nvariables individually as opposed to all together. If both bond\nprices and interest rates are affected by changes in the\ninflation rates, the results of the sensitivity analysis may be\ndistorted.","sectionId":"20.1"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1363","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":56,"question":"56) An analyst completed a sensitivity analysis for sales and\nprepared the following graph:\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nBased on the graph, which of the following is\nthe most appropriate conclusion?","options":["If the company has less than $2,000 to spend, advertising\nexpenses has the lowest impact on sales compared to\npackaging expenses and R&D expenses.","If the company has $2,000 to spend on one of the listed cost\ncategories it should spend it on packaging to maximize sales.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","R&D expenses has the highest impact on sales compared to\npackaging expenses and advertising expenses.","If the company has $6,500 to spend on one of the listed cost\ncategories it should spend it on R&D to maximize sales."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Sensitivity analysis uses trial and error to determine the effects\nof changes in variables or assumptions on final results. It is\nuseful in deciding whether expending additional resources to\nobtain better forecasts is justified. According to the graph, if\nthe company has more than $5,000 to spend on one of the\nlisted cost categories, it should spend it on R&D to maximize\nsales.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1364","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":57,"question":"57) A local insurance company has observed a dramatic increase\nin claims in recent years that the actuarial and risk control\ndepartments failed to explain. To identify the reason, the\ncompany gathered demographic and customer information and\nidentified that married women aged 50 or older, who were\npresumed to be low-risk customers, have been filing more\nclaims than expected. This is an example of","options":["Predictive analysis.","Data mining analysis.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data","What-if analysis.","Sensitivity analysis."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Data mining is the search for unexpected relationships among\ndata. The classic example of the use of data mining was the\ndiscovery by convenience stores that diapers and beer often\nappeared on the same sales transaction in the late evening.\nThus, identifying a previously unknown pattern (i.e., the\nunexpected higher claims by customers presumed to be low-\nrisk) is an example of data mining.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1365","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":58,"question":"58) Which of the following is not an activity or analysis typically\nperformed during the data mining process?","options":["Prescriptive analysis.","Anomaly detection.","Regression analysis.","Data visualization."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Prescriptive analysis concentrates on what an organization\nneeds to do in order for the predicted future results to actually\noccur. The data mining process involves (1) finding anomalies,\n(2) finding relationships between variables and clustering, (3)\ngeneralizing the relationships, (4) performing regression\nanalysis to quantify the relationships, and (5) data\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nvisualization. The data mining process does not include\nidentifying and suggesting what should be done.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"v2-su20-q1366","volume":2,"unit":20,"unitTitle":"Systems Development and Data Analytics","subunit":null,"questionNumber":59,"question":"59) A company has three production departments – A, B, and C.\nBased on production data, the production manager of\nproduction department A found that the defective rate for the\ncurrent month is 6% greater than expected. To identify the\nreason for the deviation, the production manager asked for\nhelp from the management accountant, who then gathered\nproduction-related information, developed a model, and found\nthe relationships among the defective rates and various\nvariables. Seeing that production departments B and C are\nalso experiencing a higher-than-expected defective rate, the\naccountant applied the model to production departments B and\nC to see if the relationships can be generalized. Results of the\nanalyses were summarized and presented to senior\nmanagement, who then developed plans to mitigate the\nproblem.\n\n2: Analytics and Big Data\nWhich of the following phases from the above scenario\nis not part of the data mining process?","options":["Finding that the defective rate is 6% greater than expected.","Applying the model to other production departments.","Presenting the results to senior management.","Developing plans to mitigate the problem."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The data mining process includes the tasks from anomaly\ndetection to the presentation of data. Activities after the\npresentation of data, such as developing plans based on the\npresented data, are not part of in the data mining process.","sectionId":"20.2"},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.001_1905","question":"How is a next-generation firewall (NGFW) different from a traditional firewall?","options":["There is no difference; this is more of a marketing term.","Next-generation firewalls are a newer technology, are only available as a hardware appliance, and allow for stateful inspection.","Next-generation firewalls are specifically designed to separate only trusted networks utilizing newer technologies.","Next-generation firewalls combine traditional firewall features with the addition of other advanced features, including application filtering."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Next-generation firewalls (NGFWs) incorporate not only traditional firewall features but more advanced features like application filtering—being able to determine if the application being used through the firewall is in fact that application.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.006_1905","question":"Regarding cyberattacks, which of the following refers to data hijacking?","options":["Firmware attack","Groupware attack","Middleware attack","Ransomware attack"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Ransomware has everything to do with data hijacking. Scammers and data-kidnappers send emails to innocent users that look like courtesy messages from legitimate companies—especially shipping companies—to spread the malicious software (malware) called ransomware botnet. Ransomware works by encrypting all the files on a user's computer (e.g., photos, documents, and tax refunds) that the user has saved to the hard drive or to any shared folders. Once the files are encrypted, the user will not be able to open the files without the decryption key, which the user can get only from the criminals behind the ransomware. Hackers or criminals hijack the data files and hold the user files “hostage,” often encrypting them and demanding payment, typically in bitcoins, for the user to get the files back.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.022_1905","question":"Regarding cyberattacks, identity thieves can get personal information through which of the following means?","options":["I only","III only","I and III","I, II, III, and IV"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Identity thieves get personal information by stealing records or information while they are on the job, bribing an employee who has access to these records, hacking electronic records, and conning information out of employees. Sources of personal information include dumpster diving, which includes rummaging through personal trash, a business's trash, or public trash dumps. Skimming includes stealing credit card or debit card numbers by capturing the information in a data storage device. Phishing and pretexting deal with stealing information through email or phone by posing as legitimate companies and claiming that you have a problem with your account. This practice is known as phishing online or pretexting (social engineering) by phone respectively. Pretext callers who are fraudsters use pieces of a customer's personal information to impersonate an account holder to gain access to that individual's account information. Armed with personal information, such as an individual's name, address, and Social Security number, a pretext caller may try to convince a bank's employee to provide confidential account information. While pretext calling may be difficult to spot, there are measures banks can take to reduce the incidence of pretext calling, such as limiting the circumstances under which customer information may be disclosed by telephone. A bank's policy could be that customer information is disclosed only through email, text message, a letter, or in-person meeting.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.007_1905","question":"From a software vulnerability point of view, which one of the following items is different from the other three items?","options":["Zero-day attacks","Zero-day warez","Zero-day exploits","Zero-day incidents"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A zero-day warez (negative day) refers to software, games, videos, music, or data unlawfully released or obtained on the day of public release. Either a hacker or an employee of the releasing company is involved in copying on the day of the official release. A zero-day warez is different from a zero-day attack, a zero-day exploit, and a zero-day incident.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.004_1905","question":"Which of the following would best describe a Pentest (Penetration Test)?","options":["Assign your IT (Information Technology) Team to check for vulnerabilities in your firewall, omitting the need for Social Engineering techniques.","Fix what is discovered during a routine vulnerability scan of your network and systems, including those related to phone system exploits.","Contract with an external company to assess the current state of your firewall and provide a detailed synopsis of its configuration along with a plan to take corrective action.","Contract with an external company to essentially gain access to potentially high-valued systems within your company."],"answer":"D","explanation":"A Pentest is best conducted by an external company that knows very little about your network and systems (called a black-box test). As part of the engagement, reconnaissance plays a major role which may uncover information previously deemed innocuous that could lead to social engineering opportunities that could allow access into a system.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.005_1905","question":"In order to detect and thwart cyberattacks, which of the following controls provides the strongest level of security?","options":["Passwords plus PINs","Biometrics only","Passwords plus biometrics","Passwords plus biometrics plus PINs"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The combination of passwords, biometrics, and PINs provides the strongest level of security. Here, passwords provide a one-factor authentication (1FA) mechanism, biometrics provide a two-factor authentication (2FA) mechanism, and PINs provide a three-factor authentication (3FA) mechanism. In practice, a three-factor authentication (3FA) mechanism is much stronger than a 2FA or 1FA mechanism.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.014_1905","question":"Regarding cyberattacks, which of the following identifies a flaw in hardware, firmware, or software that leaves an information system open to potential exploitation by hackers and others?","options":["Fuzz testing","Beta testing","Self-assessments","Vulnerability testing"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Vulnerability testing can identify a flaw in hardware, firmware, or software that leaves an information system open to potential exploitation by hackers and others. These flaws provide opportunities for hackers to gain access to a computer system, execute computer commands as another user, or access data contrary to specified access restrictions or rules. Organizations can use automated vulnerability scanners running either continuously or periodically to scan their computer systems for known security exposures.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.011_1905","question":"Which of the following statements is true about a firewall and an intrusion detection system (IDS)?","options":["Firewalls are a substitution for an IDS.","Firewalls are an alternative to an IDS.","Firewalls are a complement to an IDS.","Firewalls are a replacement for an IDS."],"answer":"C","explanation":"An intrusion detection system (IDS) should be used as a complement to a firewall, not as a substitute, alternative, or replacement for it. Together, they provide a synergistic strong effect. A firewall is a hardware or software providing protection against outside attackers by shielding a user's computer or network from malicious or unnecessary network traffic. Firewalls can also prevent malicious software (malware) from accessing a computer or network via the Internet. Firewalls can be configured to block data from certain locations using computer network addresses, applications, or ports while allowing relevant and necessary data through using rules. An IDS is a hardware or software product that gathers and analyzes information from various areas within a computer or a network to identify possible security breaches, which include intrusions (hacker attacks from outside the organization) and misuse (employee attacks from within the organization).","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.sec.brch.005_1904","question":"Regarding cyberattacks, which of the following is not an example of a first-line-of-defense mechanism?","options":["Policies and procedures","Internal controls","Audit trails and logs","Training, awareness, and education"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Audit trails and logs provide after-the-fact information to detect anomalies and therefore cannot provide the first line of defense in terms of preventing an anomaly. Hence, audit trails and logs provide a second-line-of-defense mechanism.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.019_1905","question":"Which of the following is best to replace the use of personal identification numbers (PINs) in the world of automated teller machines (ATMs)?","options":["Iris-detection technology","Voice technology","Hand technology","Fingerprint technology"],"answer":"A","explanation":"An automated teller machine (ATM) customer can stand within three feet of a camera that automatically locates and scans the iris in the eye. The scanned barcode is then compared against previously stored code in the bank's file. Iris-detection technology is far superior for accuracy compared to the accuracy of voice, face, hand, and fingerprint identification systems. Hence, the iris technology does not require a PIN when using an ATM's services.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.008_1905","question":"Which of the following is not one of the actions taken by a firewall on a network packet?","options":["Accept","Deny","Discard","Destroy"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Destroy is not one of the actions taken by a firewall on a network packet. The firewall examines a network packet's source and destination addresses and ports, and determines what protocol is in use. From there, it starts at the top of the rule-base and works down through the rules until it finds a rule that permits (accepts) or denies the packet. Destroy is not one of the actions taken by a firewall due to firewall log.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.003_1905","question":"Penetration and vulnerability scanning are forms of what type of control?","options":["Detective","Preventive","Compensating","Corrective"],"answer":"B","explanation":"This answer is correct and is used to stop unwanted and unauthorized access from occurring.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.015_1905","question":"Which of the following statements is not true about Internet firewalls?","options":["A firewall can enforce security policy.","A firewall can log Internet activity.","A firewall can limit an organization's security exposure.","A firewall can protect against computer viruses in personal computers."],"answer":"D","explanation":"This choice is not true about firewalls. Firewalls (also known as secure gateways) cannot keep personal computer viruses out of a network. There are simply too many types of viruses and too many ways a virus can hide within data. The most practical way to address the virus problem is through host-based virus-protection software and user education concerning the dangers of viruses and precautions to take against them.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.017_1905","question":"Which one of the following items is not intrinsically a computer crime or even a misdeed?","options":["Wiretapping","Eavesdropping","Super-zapping","Masquerading"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. Super-zapping, a utility program in the IBM mainframe computer environment, can be thought of as the master key to the computer system. It unlocks most of the security safeguards and integrity controls. In the wrong hands, its use can be damaging. Use of supervisor privileges, root privileges, or the running of programs that bypass security controls is needed to troubleshoot certain operating system problems. In other words, super-zapping can be used for both good and bad purposes. The problem is that no audit trail exists.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.023_1905","question":"Regarding cyberattacks, pharming attacks are an example of which of the following?","options":["Browser-based attacks","Server-based attacks","Network-based attacks","User-based attacks"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Internet-related threats are broken down into three categories: browser-based, server-based, and network-based attacks. Pharming attack is an example of network-based attack. An attacker may modify the domain name system (DNS) mechanism to direct it to a false website. These techniques are often used to perform pharming attacks, where users may divulge sensitive information. Note that pharming attacks can also be initiated by subverting the victim's host computer files.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.018_1905","question":"Regarding cybersecurity, which of the following is not a core part of defense-in-depth strategy?","options":["Least functionality","Layered protections","System partitioning","Lines-of-defense"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Least functionality is not a core part of the defense-in-depth strategy. Least functionality or minimal functionality means configuring an information system to provide only essential capabilities and specifically prohibiting or restricting the use of risky (by default) and unnecessary functions, ports, protocols, and/or services. However, it is sometimes convenient to provide multiple services from a single component of an information system, but doing so increases risk over limiting the services provided by any one component. Where feasible, IT organizations limit component functionality to a single function per device (e.g., e-mail server or Web server, not both). Because least functionality deals with system usability, it cannot support the defense-in-depth strategy (i.e., protecting from security breaches).","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.sec.brch.001_1904","question":"The addition of encrypting data in transit (i.e. HTTPS) that was previously encrypted at rest is a form of what type of control?","options":["Detective","Preventive","Compensating","Corrective"],"answer":"C","explanation":"A Compensating control is deployed to augment or enhance existing controls.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.021_1905","question":"Regarding cyberattacks, what do fundamental goals or elements of the defense-in-depth strategy include?","options":["Sneak-and-peek","Trap-and-trace","Detect-and-respond","Protect-and-detect"],"answer":"C","explanation":"A fundamental tenet of the defense-in-depth strategy is to prevent a cyberattack from penetrating networks and to detect and respond effectively to mitigate the effects of attacks that do. Detect-and-respond capabilities are complex structures that run the gamut of intrusion and attack detection, characterization, and response. Defense in depth is an information security strategy integrating people, technology, and operations capabilities to establish variable barriers across multiple layers and dimensions of information systems. It is an approach for establishing an adequate information assurance (IA) posture whereby (1) IA solutions integrate people, technology, and operations; (2) IA solutions are layered within and among IT assets; and (3) IA solutions are selected based on their relative level of robustness. Implementation of this approach recognizes that the highly interactive nature of information systems and enclaves creates a shared risk environment; therefore, the adequate assurance of any single asset is dependent on the adequate assurance of all interconnecting assets. It is an information protection strategy dealing with controls placed at multiple levels and at multiple places in a given system. It supports agile defense strategy and is the same as security in depth. Defense in depth is a security control.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.sec.brch.004_1904","question":"Regarding cyberattacks, which of the following uses only approved and qualified testers to conduct real-world attacks against a computer system or network?","options":["Proxy testing","Penetration testing","Alpha testing","Fault-injection testing"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Penetration testing is the process of using approved personnel to conduct real-world attacks against a computer system or network to identify and correct security weaknesses or flaws (security holes) before they are discovered and exploited by others such as outsiders (hackers) and insiders (disgruntled employees).","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.009_1905","question":"Which of the following is well qualified to conduct a penetration testing on an organization's security posture?","options":["Blue team","Audit team","Red team","White team"],"answer":"C","explanation":"A penetration testing is laboratory-based testing consisting of (1) pretest analysis based on full knowledge of the target system, (2) pretest identification of potential vulnerabilities based on pretest analysis, and (3) current testing designed to determine exploitability of identified vulnerabilities. A red team is a group of people authorized and organized to emulate a potential adversary's attack or exploitation capabilities against an enterprise's security posture by conducting penetration testing.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.012_1905","question":"Regarding cyberattacks, adware is responsible for which of the following?","options":["Scanning attacks","Skimming attack","Smurf attack","Malvertizing attack"],"answer":"D","explanation":"An adware is any software program intended for marketing purposes, such as to deliver and display advertising banners or pop-ups to the user's computer screen or to track the user's online usage or purchasing activity. Adware tracks a user's activity and passes it to third parties without the user's knowledge or consent. Click fraud is possible with adware because it involves deceptions and scams that inflate advertising bills with improper usage and charges per click in online web advertisements. A malvertizing attack is the use of malicious advertisements (ads) on legitimate websites. These ads contain a programing code that will infect a user's computer without any action required from the user (i.e., the user does not have to click on the ad to become infected). Adware, which is a form of malware, can conduct malvertizing attacks.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.013_1905","question":"Which of the following types of cyber-threat intelligence information sharing practices among user organizations can help better understand the behavior of threat actors such as hackers?","options":["Threat indicators","Security alerts","Threat tactics","Threat reports"],"answer":"C","explanation":"A cyber-threat intelligence effort is the acquisition and analysis of information to identify, track, and predict cyber-capabilities, intentions, and activities that offer courses of actions to enhance decision making. Threat intelligence is threat information that has been aggregated, transformed, analyzed, interpreted, or enriched to provide the necessary context for decision-making processes. Threat tactics, techniques, and procedures describe the behavior of a threat actor such as a hacker.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.002_1905","question":"Security controls mitigate a wide variety of information security risks. Security Awareness Training would best fall under which of the following controls?","options":["Compensating and Corrective","Preventive and Deterrent","Preventive","Corrective"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Security Awareness training is both a Preventive and Deterrent control. As a Preventive control it stops unauthorized or unwanted activity from occurring, and as a Deterrent control it discourages the same type of activities.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.sec.brch.002_1904","question":"Which of the following best describes the purpose of an advanced firewall?","options":["This security device is limited to stateful inspection of network traffic but can allow the addition of other features to discourage access into the corporate network.","It allows communication between two trusted networks.","It allows communication between two unknown networks.","It is a network security component that monitors, regulates, and provides a barrier for incoming and outgoing network traffic between a trusted and untrusted network by using features such as application filtering."],"answer":"D","explanation":"This best explains an advanced firewall from the aspect of application filtering, the ability to determine whether the application traversing the firewall is actually as advertised.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.016_1905","question":"For biometric accuracy, which of the following defines the point at which the false rejection rates and the false acceptance rates are equal?","options":["Type I error","Type II error","Crossover error rate","False non-match rate"],"answer":"C","explanation":"In biometrics, crossover error rate is defined as the point at which the false rejection rates and the false acceptance rates are equal. A goal is to obtain a low crossover error rate because it represents high accuracy, not a high crossover error rate because it represents low accuracy.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.010_1905","question":"Regarding cyberattacks, which of the following can record the source Internet Protocol (IP) address that was used to attack?","options":["Firewall logs","Network intrusion detection system logs","File integrity checking software logs","Application software logs"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Evidence of a computer security incident may be captured in several logs. Each log may contain different types of data regarding the incident. For example, a firewall log may contain the source Internet Protocol (IP) address that was used to attack.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.sec.brch.003_1904","question":"Which security control is involved with Business Continuity?","options":["Recovery","Directive","Preventive","Detective"],"answer":"A","explanation":"As an extension of Corrective Controls, Recovery Controls usually have more complex abilities which will encompass Disaster Recovery (DR) and Business Continuity (BC) processes.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sec.brch.020_1905","question":"Which one of the following advanced firewalls is most secure?","options":["Packet filtering firewall","Screened subnet firewall","Screened host firewall","Dual-homed gateway firewall"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The screened subnet firewall adds an extra layer of security by creating a network where the bastion host resides. Often called a perimeter network, the screened subnet firewall separates the internal network from the external network. Acting as a perimeter network, if there is an attack on the firewall, the attacker is restricted to the perimeter (external) network and therefore is not attacking the internal network. This leads to a stronger security. Conceptually, the screened subnet firewall is similar to a dual-homed gateway firewall, except that an entire network, rather than a single host, is reachable from the outside. It can be used to locate each component of the firewall on a separate system, thereby increasing throughput and flexibility.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.005_1905","question":"Which of the following can represent a single point-of-failure for host computer applications platform?","options":["Cloud computing","Grid computing","Utility computing","Quantum computing"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Cloud computing, which is a form of distributed computing, can become a single point-of-failure due to failure of cloud components such as storage services, network devices, database clusters, and network upgrades for the applications hosted on a cloud platform. It is called a single point of failure because all the known risks associated with all the components are concentrated in one place. This means, if one cloud component fails, the entire cloud system fails. In such situations, the services of a second cloud provider could be used to back up data processed by the primary (first) provider to ensure that during a prolonged disruption or serious disaster at the primary site, the data remains available for immediate resumption of critical operations. Note that both the user's data and essential security services may reside in and be managed within the cloud network.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.007_1905","question":"In blockchain technology, core smart contract features provide which of the following?","options":["Guaranteed execution results for all network nodes","Privacy for sensitive data","Confidentiality through encryption","Anonymity through identity disintermediation"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The blockchain implementation guarantees that smart contracts execute the same way and produce the same output on each blockchain network node. That guarantee means each node can locally verify that all transactions are valid.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.002_1905","question":"Which of the following essential characteristics of a cloud computing environment operates on a pay-per-use basis?","options":["On-demand self-service","Rapid elasticity","Resource pooling","Measured service"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Cloud providers and vendors provide a shared pool of computing resources to users and consumers and include access to networks, servers, storage, applications, and services. These resources are measured and operated on a pay-per-use basis or a charge-per-use basis. Resource usage can be monitored, controlled, and reported, thus providing transparency for both the user and provider of the utilized service.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.010_1905","question":"Prior to participating in a bitcoin's initial coin offering (ICO), a potential investor should assess and evaluate which of the following most?","options":["Right to own","Right to receive refunds","Right to resell","Right to recover"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The right to recover the invested money in the event of investment fraud or financial crime is the most important thing to assess and evaluate during an ICO offering. Bitcoins being a new investment opportunity in the financial markets, investment fraud schemes and scams are becoming a common thing happening to cheat and deceive innocent investors.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.inn.app.001_1904","question":"Cloud computing environment deals with security downside issues and security upside issues. Which of the following is an example of a security downside issue?","options":["Staff specialization","Platform strength","System complexity","Backup and recovery"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. System complexity is an example of security downside issue after knowing that security and privacy matters are the two major concerns. System security gets harder as the system complexity increases, meaning that complex systems require greater amounts of and higher levels of security measures.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.008_1905","question":"Which of the following is not a common application of bitcoin currency?","options":["Handling accounts payable or receivable transactions","Raising new capital in the primary market","Trading traditional securities in the secondary market","Trading precious metals in the secondary market"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Bitcoins are virtual tokens or virtual coins, which are virtual currencies that can be resold to others in a secondary market on a virtual currency exchange or other platforms. However, virtual currencies are not yet used to buy the traditional securities such as stocks and bonds in the secondary market.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.001_1905","question":"Which of the following defines a model for enabling a convenient and on-demand network access to a shared pool of configurable computing resources?","options":["Cluster computing model","Cloud computing model","Client-server model","Distributed computing model"],"answer":"B","explanation":"This is the definition of cloud computing where it represents a model for enabling ubiquitous, convenient, on-demand network access to a shared pool of configurable computing resources (e.g., networks, servers, storage, applications, and services) that can be rapidly provisioned and released with minimal management effort or service provider interaction.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.003_1905","question":"All of the following are defining characteristics of cloud computing that support the business rationale of improving efficiency except:","options":["On-demand resources","Connectivity from anywhere","Rapid elasticity","Usage metering"],"answer":"D","explanation":"While usage meter is a cloud computing characteristic, usage metering does not provide the organization with gained efficiency; rather the metering gives teams real-time visibility into how much computing resources are being utilized.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.006_1905","question":"Which of the following best describes a software application that is hosted by a cloud service provider accessible over a secure Internet connection?","options":["Hybrid cloud","Platform as a service (PaaS)","Private cloud","Software as a service (SaaS)"],"answer":"D","explanation":"This is the correct answer and is usually provided as a web-based application accessible over a secure Internet connection.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.009_1905","question":"Major risks in issuing an initial coin offering (ICO) for bitcoins include which of the following?","options":["I only","I and III","I, II, and IV","I, II, III, and IV"],"answer":"D","explanation":"All choices represent major risks in issuing an initial coin offering (ICO) for bitcoins. There are no traditional financial institutions (e.g., banks) involved with virtual currency transactions or ICOs, thus making it more difficult to follow the flow of money. There is no third-party custodian holding the virtual currency in case of freezing or securing the investor funds by law enforcement officials. Note that virtual currency wallets are encrypted and unlike money held in a bank or brokerage account, virtual currency cannot be frozen or seized. There is no central authority to collect virtual currency user information such as the names of the investors and traders and their physical and electronic locations. Moreover, there is no easy access to third-party business partners located outside the United States.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.inn.app.003_1904","question":"A computer code used in bitcoins or blockchain is referred to as which of the following?","options":["Crowdfunding contract","Smart contract","Unilateral contract","Bilateral contract"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. A computer code used to automate the issuance of virtual tokens or virtual coins is called smart contract. The smart contract is not a physical contract usually seen on a paper; instead, it is an electronic contract residing on a computer. A decentralized autonomous organization, called a virtual organization, issues these virtual tokens or virtual coins to investors to raise new capital. Simply stated, computer code bits generate invisible bitcoins.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.inn.app.005_1904","question":"Which of the following cloud computing deployment models operate on the premises of a cloud provider?","options":["Private cloud model","Community cloud model","Public cloud model","Hybrid cloud model"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. The public cloud model exists on the premises of a cloud provider. The nature of cloud computing infrastructure is that there is a sense of location independence in that the user-consumer generally has no detailed knowledge of or control over the exact location of the cloud vendor provided resources. This means that the resources (e.g., hardware, software, and staff) can come from anywhere and at any time. However, the user-consumer may have the higher-level knowledge of the location in terms of country, state, or datacenter. The public cloud model can be provisioned for open use by the general public. It may be owned, managed, and operated by a business, academic, or governmental organization, or some combination of them.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.004_1905","question":"Regarding data sanitization practices in a cloud computing environment, which of the following is affected most when data from one subscriber is physically commingled with the data of other subscribers?","options":["Data at rest","Data in transit","Data in use","Data to recover"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The data sanitization practices have serious implications for data security and data recovery in the cloud computing environment and are the ones most affected. Sanitization is the removal of sensitive data from a storage device such as (i) when a storage device is removed from service or moved elsewhere to be stored, (ii) when residual data remains upon termination of service, and (iii) when backup copies are made for recovery and restoration of service. Data sanitization matters can get complicated when data from one subscriber is physically commingled (data mingling) with the data of other subscribers. It is also possible to recover data from failed drives (e.g., hard drives and flash drives) that are not disposed of properly by cloud providers.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.inn.app.004_1904","question":"All of the following statements are true about bitcoins and blockchains except:","options":["Blockchains use a distributed ledger","Blockchains use a centralized ledger","Blockchains use a decentralized ledger","Blockchains use a community ledger"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. Blockchains do not use a centralized ledger. A blockchain is an electronic distributed ledger or list of entries—much like a stock ledger—that is maintained by various participants in a network of computers (i.e., community ledger). Blockchains use cryptography to process and verify transactions on the ledger, providing comfort to users and potential users of the blockchain that entries are secure. Some examples of blockchain are the Bitcoin and Ethereum blockchains, which are used to create and track transactions in bitcoin and ether, respectively. This distributed ledger is a chronological listing of all business transactions in one place to provide a clear and complete picture of all transactions.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"AQ.inn.app.002_1904","question":"In a cloud computing environment, which of the following service models allows a user-consumer to use a cloud provider's application system or program running on the provider's cloud infrastructure?","options":["Software as a service (SaaS)","Platform as a service (PaaS)","Infrastructure as a service (IaaS)","Technology as a service (TaaS)"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Correct. Software as a service (SaaS) is the capability provided to a user-consumer is to use the provider's application system or program running on a cloud infrastructure consisting of hardware and software. The user-consumer does not manage or control the underlying cloud provider's infrastructure, including network, servers, operating system, storage, or individual applications software. These applications are accessible from various user devices through a web browser, web-based email, or a program interface. An advantage of the SaaS model is that the user-consumer does not need to invest his time and money in developing or acquiring a separate application system or program because he could use the provider's application system or program. A disadvantage of the SaaS is that the user-consumer does not have a full flexibility and control over the use of the provider's application system or program. Lack of a customized application system is another disadvantage.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.inn.app.011_1905","question":"Bitcoins deploy which of the following technologies?","options":["I and II","II only","II and IV","I and III"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Both blockchain and hash chain are the technologies behind the bitcoin currency. Blockchain or hash chain technology supports bitcoins where the disruptive technology is facilitating transactions between mutually distrusting entities without the need for a trusted arbiter (i.e., no trusted middleperson, intermediary, or central bank). Blockchain is a fully distributed and decentralized ledger (similar to a stock ledger) that is synchronized through consensus between entities or parties. It facilitates fully decentralized operations, processes peer-to-peer transactions, and is tamper evident and resistant. Blockchain uses a cryptographic hash function (e.g., secure hash algorithm) and digital signature algorithm in creating a continuous list of records (blocks) that are linked and secured. Hash functions are computational functions that take a variable-length data input and produce a fixed-length result (output) that can be used as evidence representing the original data. Therefore, if the hash of two messages is identical, it can be reasonably assumed that the messages are identical as well. In summary, bitcoins can be used to make payments, to receive payments, to pay for advertisements, and to purchase gift cards from a retail store. Here, the key point is that a virtual currency is exchanged for flat currency (i.e., U.S. dollars), funds, or other forms of virtual currency, all for a fee.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.010_1905","question":"All of following are limitations in time series analysis except:","options":["Framing","Over-specification","Reliance on predictions","Reliance on mechanical extrapolation"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The biggest advantage of using time series analysis is that it can be used to understand the past as well as predict the future. Business managers use time series analysis on a regular basis for sales forecasting, budgetary analysis, inventory management, and quality control.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.006_1905","question":"Which analytical model would be the best choice if a company wishes to test the prediction that is in the form of a quantity?","options":["Intelligence modeling","Regression modeling","Classification modeling","Clustering modeling"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A regression problem requires the prediction of a quantity; the regression can have real-valued or discrete input variables. Further, a regression problem where input variables are ordered by time is called a time series forecasting problem.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.002_1905","question":"A business made the decision to utilize a big data lake. Which of the following technologies would enable users to interpret the data more easily?","options":["Data visualization","Process automation","Data mining","Business intelligence"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Data visualization enables users less skilled than data scientists to interact with and explore data.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.009_1905","question":"Which of the following accurately defines the coefficient of determination?","options":["The coefficient of determination provides the degree of linear-correlation of variables (goodness of fit) in regression analysis.","The coefficient of determination provides the degree of nonlinear-correlation of variables (goodness of fit) in regression analysis.","The coefficient of determination provides the degree of linear-correlation of variables (goodness of fit) in sensitivity analysis.","The coefficient of determination provides the degree of nonlinear-correlation of variables (goodness of fit) in sensitivity analysis."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Also known as R2, the coefficient of determination is a statistical measure of how close the data is to the fitted regression line. R2 closer to 0% indicates that the model explains none of the variability of the response data around its mean.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.bus.int.005_1905","question":"Which of the following describes a typical use-case for the utilization of a business intelligence (BI) solution?","options":["BI enables organizations to utilize a mobile device to conduct payroll processing.","Accounts payable and accounts receivable systems are consolidated into a single dashboard to highlight delinquent versus diligent customers that pay invoices on-time.","Accounts payable approval activity is streamlined in the solution by rules-based, auto-approved, workflow criteria that limits human involvement to specific approval situations.","A portal for internal audit to save their workpapers and other key pieces of evidence from fieldwork is a typical use-case."],"answer":"B","explanation":"A dashboard providing consolidated and correlated data is a typical use-case for a BI solution.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.bus.int.003_1905","question":"During the progression of data, which of the following best describes the insight phase?","options":["When the initial information is collected for analysis, deciding on which format to utilize for the assessment","When the information allocated is converted into actionable steps that can be taken (i.e., directions)","When knowledge based on discoveries in data analysis and the relationships between variables or correlation is acquired","The ability to increase effectiveness of information. This phase attempts to add value, which requires the mental function that we call judgment."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Insight converts data and information into correlations in order to identify relationships within the data (i.e., retail sales increase when certain environmental triggers occur).","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.bus.int.004_1905","question":"During big-data collection efforts, which of the following requires extra attention?","options":["Timing of data","Sourcing of data","Quality of data","Scope of data"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. Sourcing of data is a critical consideration because real and fake sources exist and because there are so many data sources, thus making it difficult to know what is good or bad information. Hence, data sources require extra attention.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.bus.int.002_1905","question":"Which of the following is an example of unstructured data?","options":["Data in disconnected computer systems","Data in data warehouses","Data in databases","Web pages on the Internet"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Correct. Data in disconnected computer systems is unstructured due to multiple and dissimilar systems collecting data with different data formats and with different data structures. Unstructured data consists of external data sources with free-form format.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.005_1905","question":"This type of analytics provides information such as risk, performance, or problem indicators. Choose the best answer.","options":["Diagnostic analytics","Predictive analytics","Prescriptive analytics","Descriptive analytics"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Diagnostic analytics provides end users or organizations with root cause indicators to assist in solving problems or improving processes.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.bus.int.001_1905","question":"Which of the following characteristics of big data is the major technical driver of investment in big data?","options":["Volume","Velocity","Veracity","Variety"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Correct. Variety is the major technical driver of investment in big data because more variety means more insights, more decisions, and more opportunities. The variety of data comes from all types of data formats such as structured and unstructured and from all types of data sources such as internal and external.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.003_1905","question":"Business intelligence software can be used to create which of the following to turn raw data into actionable information?","options":["I and II","II and III","III and IV","I, II, III, and IV"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. Business intelligence (BI) is collecting and analyzing internal data and external data to provide new insights that were not apparent before. Both pivot table and contingency table are used to turn raw data into actionable information. A pivot table is a second, revised table in rows and columns containing reformatted data using the raw data from the first, original table in rows and columns. A pivot table is also called a pivot chart. First Table → Original Table Second Table → Pivot Table The basic data values are the same between the original tale and the pivot table. However, the pivot table contains sorted, rearranged, and summarized data, providing better insights. For example, a retail marketing manager can create a pivot table showing which salesperson has the highest sales dollars in a given month or quarter from original sales data tables. A contingency table is a type of table presented in a matrix format displaying frequency distribution, showing their probabilities. Contingency tables (cross-tabulations) are used in business intelligence, market research, and customer surveys where interrelations and interactions between two or more variables can be studied to obtain greater insights of data. Due to their statistical focus, contingency tables show a measure of association between variables. For example, a table can be put together showing how male and female customers prefer to purchase product A and product B from a retailer.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.007_1905","question":"Suppose Dana Sunderson works as a data analyst for Ellen Votemein, who is running for a state office. Ms. Votemein has asked Ms. Sunderson to take statewide voter demographic information and predict whether any voter will vote for one of two political parties (and which one), or will not vote for either party. The model should also provide information on which features would most likely influence a voter to vote for Ms. Votemein, without being concerned about model overfitting.","options":["Clustering","Logistic regression","Decision tree","Linear regression"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Logistic regression supports predictive queries and is generally less susceptible to overfitting. Logistic regression can also be used for prescriptive modeling.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.011_1905","question":"All of following are limitations in linear regression analysis except:","options":["Linear regression assesses at the mean of the dependent variable.","It indicates impact of independent variables.","Linear regression is responsive to outliers.","The linear data is independent."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Regression analysis enables analysts to compare the effects of independent variables measured on different scales, such as the effect of price changes and the number of promotional activities. These benefits help data scientists to eliminate and evaluate the best set of variables to be used for building predictive models.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.001_1905","question":"Which of the following would be the best answer that describes a business reason to utilize Data Analytics?","options":["An organization wishes to automate processes such as repetitive data entry that are entered via OCR scanning of documents and input into the respective fields.","The CFO and Controller want to see daily reports in the form of dashboards outlining cash flow, accounts receivable, accounts payable, etc.","Internal investigations requests to have the capability to forensically assess data to determine if fraud or corrupt practices are being carried out.","An organization wishes to assess a large volume of data for trends, filtering, and visualization in order to make the information easier to comprehend."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Data analytics will empower the business to intake a large amount of data to make intelligent decisions based on the trends identified.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.004_1905","question":"All of the following are appropriate use cases for data analytics except:","options":["Automating risk management","Managing customer data","Fraud detection","Data classification"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Data classification describes the process and corresponding policies to classify data based on its sensitivity to the business, regulators, or its customers.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.bus.int.008_1905","question":"Which of the following elements in a regression equation represents the Dependent Variable?","options":["Y","X","b","a"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Y is the value of the Dependent Variable in a regression equation; this element is what is being predicted or explained.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.007_1905","question":"From a software testing viewpoint, when does a formal change control mechanism start in a system development project?","options":["After completion of integration testing","After completion of unit testing","After completion of systems testing","After completion of acceptance testing"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Integration testing is the cutoff point for the development project, and, after integration, it is labeled as the back-end testing. Integration means various parts and components of the system are integrated to form the entire software product. The product is under formal change control after completion of integration testing. Specifically, after integration testing, every change of the software must have a specific reason and must be documented and tracked.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.011_1905","question":"Which of the following is not an example of a first line-of-defense?","options":["Physical security","Network monitors","Software testing","Quality assurance"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Software testing in a new system development project provides a last line-of-defense because it is the last step to ensure proper functioning of the new system. After testing, the system is implemented and ready to operate.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.sys.dev.lc.001_1904","question":"Which phase of the System Development Lifecycle will require the most interaction with the business to validate needs?","options":["Planning","Analysis","Design","Deployment"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The Analysis phase is synonymous with the assessment of business requirements to validate that stakeholder needs are being met throughout the project.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.006_1905","question":"What is the correct sequence of application software testing in a system development project?","options":["Integration test, unit test, systems test, acceptance test","Unit test, systems test, integration test, acceptance test","Acceptance test, unit test, integration test, systems test","Unit test, integration test, systems test, acceptance test"],"answer":"D","explanation":"This choice is the correct sequence. A system development life cycle (SDLC) moves through the unit test, integration test, system test, and acceptance test in that sequence. Programmers perform both the unit test and integration tests, whereas system testing is conducted jointly between users and programmers. End users (accounting staff) and IT production operations staff, from their own viewpoint, perform acceptance testing. The quality of a computer-based application system is enhanced if this sequence is followed during software testing.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.009_1905","question":"Which of the following software testing levels is least understood by system developers and end users in a system development project?","options":["Integration testing","Unit testing","System testing","Module testing"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Integration testing is conducted when specific software units are integrated with other software units or with system components. Its objective is to test the interfaces among separately tested program units. Software integration tests check how the units interact with other software (for example, libraries) and hardware. Integration testing is in the middle; it is neither unit testing nor system testing. The approach to integration testing varies such as top-down, bottom-up, a combination of top-down and bottom-up (sandwich), or all-at-once (big-bang) approaches. The variety of ways the integration testing can be conducted and the fact that there is no base document such as specifications to rely upon for testing create difficulty in understanding the objectives of integration testing clearly. End users are accounting and finance staff. In essence, an integration testing is performed after unit testing to examine how program units would interface and interact with each.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.004_1905","question":"All of the following are advantages of using blockchain technology except:","options":["Blockchain uses protected cryptography to secure the data ledgers. Also, the current ledger is dependent on its adjacent completed block to complete the cryptography process.","The transactions that take place are transparent. The individuals who are provided authority can view the transaction.","The transactions stored in the blocks are contained in millions of computers participating in the chain. Hence it is decentralized.","The data structure in a blockchain is append-only. So, the data can be altered or deleted."],"answer":"D","explanation":"While it is true that the data structure in blockchain is append-only, the last statement in this option is misleading, the data cannot be altered or deleted once the transaction is authorized.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.002_1905","question":"Which of the following phases of the System Development Lifecycle can be best described as the project plan is put into motion and the work of the project is performed?","options":["Maintenance","Design","Implementation","Analysis"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The Implementation Phase involves putting the project plan into action. The activities required to build each deliverable will be clearly specified within the project requirements document and project plan.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.001_1905","question":"Which phase of the Software Development Lifecycle would involve the allocation of resource requirements, budgeting, agreement on timeline, and the definition of key milestones for the software development project?","options":["Planning","Development","Maintenance","Testing"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The planning phase involves the planning of resource requirements, budgeting, timeline, and key milestones for the software development project.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.010_1905","question":"In a system development life cycle (SDLC), which of the following tests is driven by system requirements?","options":["Black-box testing","White-box testing","Gray-box testing","Glass-box testing"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Black-box testing, also known as functional testing, executes part or all the system to validate that the user requirements and system requirements are satisfied. Because the unit test is the first test conducted, its scope should be comprehensive enough to include both types of testing, that is, both black-box testing and white-box testing.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.014_1905","question":"Which of the following describes a financial administrative activity that is currently carried out manually that is a candidate for process automation?","options":["The organization's Controller and CFO receive a dashboard containing quarterly results.","The creation of a P&L report is generated using bots rather than humans to allocate and aggregate the data to be presented.","Credit card payment chargebacks are automatically adjusted on monthly sales reports.","Customer data is automatically encrypted upon form entry within the organization's website."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Typically the process to create a P&L report has been traditionally manual, whereas the utilization of bots can automate the entire report creation process.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.013_1905","question":"Which of the following most closely describes the automation of invoice pre-processing?","options":["Processing systems can incorporate invoices that originated in an assortment of formats: by scanning a physical document, by reading contents of an email or electronic fax, or by translating data from a portal upload.","By imaging the invoice upon receipt, most organizations will be able to adopt a policy of destroying the physical invoice after two or three months.","Paper-based and electronic documentation from purchasing can be captured electronically by a processing system for use in later stages of the procure-to-pay process.","Automating the routing of approval flows, verifying accounting codes, and providing interfaces to match against POs and open receipts."],"answer":"A","explanation":"These steps would occur prior to the invoice being fully processed on the system, thus describing the automation of invoice pre-processing.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.sys.dev.lc.003_1904","question":"All of the following are phases within the Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC) except:","options":["Systems analysis","Conceptual design","Workflow knowledge transfer","Operations and maintenance"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Workflow knowledge transfer is not a phase within the SDLC. The phases of the SDLC are system analysis, conceptual design, physical design, implementation and conversion, and operations and maintenance.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.008_1905","question":"Effective controls during the application software-testing activities in a system development project include which of the following?","options":["Test cases and test documentation","Test summaries and test execution reports","Activity logs, incident reports, and software versioning","Test cases rejected and test cases accepted"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Activity logs contain a record of all the test cases executed. Incident reports show a priority assigned to test problems during test execution. All incidents logged should be resolved within a reasonable time. Software versioning controls the program source versions to ensure that there is no duplication or confusion between multiple versions.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.012_1905","question":"All of the following are an AICPA Trusted Service Category (TSC) for SOC2 Attestation except:","options":["Security","Confidentiality","Accountability","Processing Integrity"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Accountability is not one of the AICPA Trusted Service Categories. The TSC are Security, Confidentiality, Processing Integrity, Availability, and Privacy.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.sys.dev.lc.005_1904","question":"Which of following categories would contain attributes to gauge if a process would be an ideal candidate for a process automation?","options":["Process relevance","Process suitability","Process governance","Process scope"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Attributes such as repetitiveness of process, stability, and how the data is structured would illustrate the suitability of the process being a candidate for automation.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.016_1905","question":"Which of the following can help in improving a computer system's performance?","options":["Root cause analysis","Prospective analysis","Retrospective analysis","Contemporary analysis"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Root causes are fundamental deficiencies or problems that result in a nonconformance, which must be corrected to prevent recurrence. Root causes link undesirable events or problems to their sources. Examples of computer system's performance-related problems include system downtime, website crashes, software glitches, slow response time for online transactions and queries, system outages, and system reboots. Measuring a problem's root causes involves determining the sources of identified risks (known risks) and understanding the positive and negative impacts of those known risks on other areas of a computer system. Corrective controls must address and reduce the root causes of problems at their source, not symptoms. Root cause analysis is a technique used to identify the conditions that initiate the occurrence of an undesirable activity, state, or an event. It identifies relevant causes and effects of problems. Root cause analysis is a part of risk management techniques and can help in improving a computer system's performance. Simply stated, root cause analysis moves past events to current events to future events.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.005_1905","question":"All of the following are true regarding static code analysis except:","options":["Static analysis is performed in a non-runtime environment.","It will inspect program code for all possible runtime behaviors.","Static code analysis is executed while a program is in operation.","Static analysis is done after coding and before executing unit tests."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Static analysis is performed in a non-runtime environment. Typically, a static analysis tool will inspect program code for all possible runtime behaviors and seek out coding flaws, backdoors, and potentially malicious code. Dynamic analysis adopts the opposite approach and is executed while a program is in operation.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.015_1905","question":"Which answer best describes Business Intelligence and Process Automation?","options":["Business Intelligence aggregates data and presents it visually in a manner that enables users to sort and filter through volumes of different data types with ease. Process automation leverages business intelligence to make decisions.","Business Intelligence aggregates data and presents it visually in a manner that enables users to sort and filter through volumes of different data types with ease. Process automation reduces the amount of time the BI data can be consumed by the end user.","Business Intelligence aggregates data and presents it visually in a manner that enables users to sort and filter through volumes of different data types with ease. Process automation gives the organizations the capability to eliminate or reduce administrative processes that were traditionally manual in nature.","Business Intelligence aggregates data and presents it visually in a manner that enables users to sort and filter through volumes of different data types with ease. Process automation encrypts sensitive information automatically."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Both statements explain BI and process automation accurately.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.sys.dev.lc.003_1905","question":"All of the following are characteristics of smart contracts except:","options":["Self-verifying","Self-enforcing","Third-party authorization","Tamper-proof"],"answer":"C","explanation":"One of the most unique features of blockchain is its quality of acting as a decentralized network which is shared between all the parties of the network, thus eliminating the involvement of middlemen or third-party intermediaries to authorize blockchain smart contracts.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.sys.dev.lc.002_1904","question":"Which of the following statements describes the “break-the-glass procedure” scenario within the SDLC?","options":["A development team is running regression testing against previously developed code.","A developer needs access to the production environment to fix a query that is causing performance issues; all his or her changes are approved subsequent to resolving the problem.","In-scope business users have direct access to a staging environment to perform acceptance testing.","A database in the production environment is having performance issues; users try to fix the problem on their own with their own tools."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It is not typical for developers to have access to production code. This in turn would merit the utilization of a break-the-glass or emergency change procedure.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.sys.dev.lc.004_1904","question":"Which of the following is a supporting document that outlines the flow of an automated process?","options":["Income statement","Decision tree","P&L Report","Project charter"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A decision tree will visually depict what steps are taken within the process flow of elements that would be automated by instructions or by bots.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.dat.min.001_1905","question":"Which of the following can uncover hidden patterns, trends, correlations, outliers, anomalies, and subtle relationships in data and help to infer rules that allow for the prediction of future results and outcomes?","options":["Web scraping","Data mining","Web mining","Social mining"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. This is the definition of data mining. Data mining is the application of database technologies and advanced data-analytics programs to uncover hidden patterns, trends, correlations, outliers, anomalies, and subtle relationships in data and to help infer rules that allow for the prediction of future results and outcomes. Data mining analyzes data for relationships that have not previously been discovered and other insights not suggested by a priori hypotheses or explicit assumptions. Big data is often used as input into data mining applications due to its vast amounts of data, meaning the more the data available, the more it can be applied to. This means that a data analyst can mine large amounts of data (big data) to reveal patterns and to provide insights. Note that data mining drives web scraping, web mining, and social mining as it is a common factor in them.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.dat.min.002_1905","question":"Which of the following databases are best suited to support big data volumes containing unstructured data (i.e., data lakes)?","options":["SQL","MongoDB","Oracle DB v11","DB2"],"answer":"B","explanation":"MongoDB is designed to support humongous databases. It's a NoSQL database with document-oriented storage, full index support, replication, and high availability.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.dat.min.004_1905","question":"What are the most influential reasons why SQL is historically the most popular data query tool?","options":["SQL has been enhanced and extended for over 40 years and contains nearly every feature analysis need to retrieve and analyze data.","SQL is an ANSI standard and is the default query language for nearly 80% of all database systems in use today.","Since ANSI adopted the SQL standard, SQL queries can be used on different vendors’ databases with virtually no modification.","SQL returns data that matches English-like criteria in the form of tables that are easy to understand and visualize."],"answer":"D","explanation":"SQL's simplicity is the most influential reason it has gained such widespread acceptance. The syntax is English-like and the data SQL returns is in a table format that is easy to understand, visualize, and import into other tools.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.dat.min.002_1905","question":"Which of the following is a key challenge for data mining?","options":["Unstructured data","Structured data","Distributed data","Voluminous data"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Real-world data is usually stored on different platforms in distributed computing environments. It could be in databases, individual systems, or even on the Internet. It is practically very difficult to bring all the data to a centralized data repository mainly due to organizational and technical reasons.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.dat.min.003_1905","question":"Which of the following fully describes the nature of data mining?","options":["I only","II only","III only","III and IV"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Correct. Data mining is an iterative and trial-and-error process in searching for the right application approach yielding the correct and expected results. It is not a straightforward and linear process of applying some formulas and equations and hoping for the best results. It is a nonlinear and iterative process until the right results are obtained. Data mining is an art in terms of knowing what data to collect, what analytical tool to apply that is appropriate to the collected data, and how to interpret the analytical results. Data mining is a science in terms of knowing what analytical model or equations fit the data (i.e., simulation or no simulation and regression analysis or no regression analysis); what the error rate or popularity of the selected analytical tool is; whether the tools are proven, tested, and trusted in the marketplace (i.e., user community); and what the level of technical sophistication of the tool is (i.e., poor, mediocre, or elegant).","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.dat.min.001_1905","question":"Which of the following can act both as a database query tool and an attacker's tool?","options":["Query by example","Ad hoc query","Structured query language","Online analytical processing"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. A query is a system-user or an end-user request for specific data from a database. Structured query language (SQL) can be used to perform a range of simple to complex database queries. SQL returns the requested data in rows and columns, similar to an Excel spreadsheet, and uses drag-and-drop graphical tools. In addition to acting as a helpful database query tool, attackers can use the SQL to act as an input injection attack tool. An attacker can craft input strings so that when the target software constructs SQL statements based on the input, the resulting SQL statement performs actions other than those the application intended. SQL injection attack enables an attacker to talk directly to the database, thus bypassing the application completely. Successful injection attacks can cause information disclosure as well as the ability to add or modify data in the database.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.dat.min.005_1905","question":"Which of the following would be an ideal use-case for analysts to mine large data sets?","options":["Network monitoring for security incidents","Perform RPA (robotic process automation) functions","To detect suspicious financial activities with a high potential risk","To perform time series analysis"],"answer":"C","explanation":"As data mining provides financial institutions with information about loan information and credit reporting, by building a model for historical customers, data can determine good and bad loans. Besides, it helps banks detect fraudulent credit card transactions that are to protect the credit card's owner.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.data.vis.003_1905","question":"Each of the following describes a benefit of using a boxplot as a visualization technique except:","options":["Provides a clear summary of the data","Effectively displays outliers","Retains and displays exact values","Handles large sets of data easily"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. Boxplots provide a simple, five-number summary of the data set consisting of the minimum value, the lower quartile, the median, the upper quartile, and the maximum value. This quick summary can be very useful, but it does not retain and display the values.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.data.vis.001_1905","question":"Best practices in utilizing tables, charts, and graphs to avoid distortion in presentation of results include which of the following?","options":["I and II","II and III","I, II, and III","I, II, III, and IV"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Correct. All four choices are correct. The basic purpose of a table, chart, or graph is to give a visual comparison between two or more things. For example, changes in budget from one year to the next may be represented in a graph. One significant reason for visualizing a comparison is to reinforce its comprehension. Charts and graphs are used to dramatize a statement, a fact, a point of view, or an idea. They are data presentation tools and visual aids assisting in the quick comprehension of simple and complex data, statistics, or problems. A chart should explain itself in silence; it should be completely understood without the assistance of a caption. The caption must act only as reinforcement to its comprehension.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.data.vis.002_1905","question":"Business data dashboards use which of the following tools to drill down in the data to a more detailed level for a better way of communicating results?","options":["Data cleansing tools","Data filtering tools","Data mingling tools","Data wrangling tools"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. Data filtering tools can be built into dashboards so data can be sliced from different perspectives or drilled down to a more detailed level using parameters such as: (1) transaction date, month, quarter, or year; (2) cost data by contract; (3) revenue or profit data by a retail store; (4) sales data by a market region; or (5) quarterly performance by a business segment. Data filters provide the ability to explore data at multiple levels and to customize user-driven data analysis. Data filters show only the requested data and ignore the rest of the data not requested.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.data.vis.004_1905","question":"Which of the following data visualization tools is used in evaluating capital investment decisions?","options":["Dot plot","Scatter diagram","Decision tree","Stem-and-leaf diagram"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. Decision trees are used in evaluating capital investment decisions. A decision tree is a graphical representation of possible alternative decisions, events, or states of nature resulting from each decision with its associated probabilities, and the outcomes of the events or states of nature. The decision problem displays the sequential nature of the decision-making situation. The decision tree has nodes, branches, and circles to represent junction boxes, connectors between the nodes, and states-of-nature nodes, respectively.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.data.vis.001_1905","question":"Which of the following data visualization tools is best to show the gaps between the current budget and previous budget?","options":["Radar chart","Box plot","Pareto chart","Part-to-whole chart"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Correct. The radar chart is a visual method to show in graphic form the size of gaps in a number of areas such as current performance versus ideal (expected) performance and current budget versus previous budget.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.data.vis.004_1905","question":"Which of the following determines the most effective channel to communicate results?","options":["Form follows function.","Quality over quantity.","Medium matches the message.","Form over substance."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. Many types of media exist to send and receive a message, including face-to-face communications, telephone calls, regular meetings and electronic meetings (videoconferencing), memos, letters, and reports. The goal is to match the media richness with the message situation. Otherwise, mismatching occurs, which can lead to confusion and embarrassment. Here, the medium is “channel” and the message is “results.” For example, management's face-to-face communications with employees is the appropriate medium to convey a company's bad-news message (e.g., employee layoffs) because it is the richest medium as it permits direct experience, multiple information cues, immediate feedback, and personal focus between management and employees. Here, face-to-face meetings with the affected employees are the preferred media to convey a bad-news message rather than mailing letters to employees (cold treatment) or the same employees reading the bad-news message in a local newspaper (very cold treatment).","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.data.vis.003_1905","question":"Which of the following data visualization tools is used to track a workflow system in a manufacturing plant or a warehouse?","options":["Histogram","Spaghetti plot","Bullet chart","Layer chart"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. A spaghetti plot (chart, diagram, or map) is a workflow system to visualize data flows through a system where flows appear as noodles. This plot is used to (1) track product routing and material movement through a factory; (2) reduce inefficiencies in an office, factory, or warehouse workflow system; and (3) show the effects of medical drugs on test patients during a new drug trial, among others. The results of a spaghetti plot can be useful in streamlining or simplifying workflow to save resources, such as time, money, materials, and energy.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.data.vis.002_1905","question":"Which of the following data visualization tools can be used as a milestone scheduling technique?","options":["Pie chart","Line chart","Gantt chart","Column chart"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. A Gantt chart is a graphical illustration of a scheduling technique. The structure of the chart shows output plotted against units of time. It does not include cost information. It highlights activities over the life of a project and contrasts actual times with projected times using a horizontal (bar) chart. It gives a quick picture of a project's progress in terms of actual time lines and projected time lines. The Gantt chart looks like a bar chart. The Gantt chart is used for milestone scheduling where each milestone has start and completion dates. A milestone represents a major activity or task to be accomplished (e.g., design phase in a computer system development project).","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ana.too.005_1905","question":"Which of the following provides the final statistical inferences and conclusions about patterns and relationships in data?","options":["Discrete data analysis","Confirmatory data analysis","Exploratory data analysis","Continuous data analysis"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. Confirmatory data analysis provides the final statistical inferences and conclusions about data patterns and relationships based on the results from exploratory data analysis. Exploratory data analysis is done first and confirmatory data analysis is done next.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ana.too.002_1905","question":"The makers of home appliances and automobiles are most impacted by which of the following components of the time-series data?","options":["Trend component","Cyclical component","Seasonal component","Irregular component"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. The makers of home appliances and automobiles are most impacted by the cyclical component of the time-series data. Cyclical fluctuations repeat themselves in a general pattern in the long term, but occur with differing frequencies and intensities. Thus, they can be isolated, but not totally predicted. Time-series analyses use past data points to project future data points and have four components: trends (upward or downward data movement), cycles (data patterns that occur every several years that tie into the business cycles), seasonality (data pattern that repeats itself periodically in weeks and months), and random variation (no data patterns shown as bumps or blips in the data that are caused by chance and unusual conditions and hence cannot be predicted). This random variation is called the irregular component.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.ana.too.005_1905","question":"Which use case represents an ideal scenario to utilize sensitivity analysis?","options":["An analyst wants a method for predicting the outcome of a decision if a situation turns out to be different compared to the key predictions.","An analyst wants to assess relative variables for bond price, inflation, and market interest rates.","An analyst wants to reduce assumptions.","An analyst wants an objective assessment of data."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Sensitivity analysis helps in analyzing how sensitive the output is by the changes in one input while keeping the other inputs constant. Sensitivity analysis works on the simple principle of “change the model and observe the behavior.”","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ana.too.006_1905","question":"“What-if” questions can be applied to all of the following except:","options":["Goal-seeking analysis","Situation analysis","Simulation techniques","Sensitivity analysis"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. “What-if” questions cannot be applied to situation analysis. This analysis deals with identifying strengths, weaknesses, opportunities, and threats (SWOT) conditions both internal and external to an organization. SWOT analysis gets information by scanning the internal and external environments of a company. “What-if” questions have nothing to do with the situation analysis because the analysis provides static answers as opposed to dynamic answers.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ana.too.001_1905","question":"Which of the following can be used when time-series data is unavailable?","options":["Clustering model","Classification model","Regression model","Confidence interval"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. Time-series analysis involves breaking down data measured over time into one or more components of trend, cyclical, seasonal, and irregular. Time-series analysis is similar to regression analysis in that both techniques help to explain the variability in data as much as possible. Regression model is a causal forecasting method that can be used to develop forecasts when time-series data are not available.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ana.too.004_1905","question":"Chi-square test is used in which of the following for testing the independence of two variables and testing hypotheses concerning proportions in a population?","options":["Standard error of the estimate","Coefficient of determination","Goodness of fit","Correlation coefficient"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Correct. Chi-square test is used for testing the independence of the two variables and testing hypotheses concerning proportions in a population. The upper tail of the Chi-square distribution is used to determine whether an observed pattern of frequencies is different from an expected pattern of frequencies. The calculated value of the Chi-square statistic will be close to zero when the observed frequencies are very close to the expected frequencies. On the other hand, the calculated static will be more than zero when the difference between these two frequencies is larger.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.ana.too.004_1905","question":"All of the following are types of time series analysis except:","options":["Trend analysis","Seasonal analysis","Cyclical analysis","Sensitivity analysis"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Sensitivity analysis is not a type of time series analysis. Sensitivity analysis is a process of varying input parameters of a model within the allowed area and observing the resulting changes in the model solution. The purpose of sensitivity analysis is to indicate the sensitivity of simulation to uncertainties in the values of input data in the model.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.ana.too.001_1905","question":"All of the following are defining characteristics of predictive analytics except:","options":["Historical patterns are utilized to output specific outcomes using algorithms.","Decisions are automated using trend data and industry insights.","The variability of the component data will have a relationship with what is likely to happen.","Analytical output provides specific recommendations to take action on."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Specific recommendations are an output of prescriptive analytics versus predictive analytics. Prescriptive analytics provide the user with actions to take in order to experience a desired outcome (i.e., based on known traffic patterns at this time, take this route to work/home).","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.ana.too.003_1905","question":"With the utilization of R2 (the coefficient of determination), of what does a result close to 100% inform the data analyst?","options":["The higher the R-squared result, the likelihood that the model fits your data is reduced.","The higher the R-squared result, the better the model fits your data. As such, this result does not explain the variability.","The higher the R-squared result, the better the model fits your data. As such, this result explains the variability.","The lower the R-squared result, the better the model fits your data. As such, this result does not explain the variability."],"answer":"C","explanation":"R-squared is a statistical measure of how close the data are to the fitted regression line. It is also known as the coefficient of determination. The higher the R-squared result, the better the model fits your data. As such, this result explains the variability.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ana.too.003_1905","question":"Which component of a time series results from short-term fluctuations in a series which are not systematic and, in some instances, not predictable?","options":["Cyclical analysis","Trend analysis","Seasonal analysis","Irregular patterns"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The irregular component of a time series results from short-term fluctuations in a series which are not systematic and, in some instances, not predictable (e.g., uncharacteristic weather patterns). Some irregular effects can, however, be expected in advance.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.ana.too.002_1905","question":"A major difference between a simple regression analysis and multiple regression analysis is which of the following?","options":["Number of dependent variables","Number of mathematical equations","Number of independent variables","Number of design experiments"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Two types of regression analysis are simple regression and multiple regression. In simple regression, there will be only two variables: one dependent variable and one independent variable. In multiple regression, there will be more than two variables: one dependent variable and more than one independent variable. Hence, the number of independent variables is the major difference between multiple regression analysis and simple regression analysis.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.2","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.proc.au.004_1904","question":"Artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) technologies can improve the efficiency and effectiveness of which of the following accounting and finance tasks?","options":["I only","II only","I and II","I, II, III, and IV"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Correct. Artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) technologies can improve the efficiency and effectiveness of accounting and finance tasks. ML, which is a part of AI technology, learns from historical data using training sets and becomes a fast learning tool. Examples of accounting and finance tasks that can be improved using ML algorithms include: Clearing payments to suppliers and vendors automatically based on historical payment data Alerting suspicious journal entries that are automatically detected to reduce fraud-related risks and noncompliance with accounting policies Completing the accounting cycles, period-ending closing schedules, and consolidated accounting statements faster to save time for the accounting staff Providing real-time insights into cash flows and liquidity levels","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb. proc.au.001_1905","question":"A business brings in a new application that performs valuation modeling. Which of the following best describes this innovative capability?","options":["The model can calculate the valuation of an asset based on user input.","The model can calculate the valuation of an asset using the 10k or 8k filing.","The model can quickly calculate the valuation of an asset using process automation.","The model can quickly calculate the valuation of an asset using data points around the asset and historical examples."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Valuation modeling enables an organization to obtain near-accurate valuations based on historical data and industry trends.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.proc.au.003_1904","question":"All of the following are benefits of robotic process automation except:","options":["Improved efficiency","Improved employee morale","Improved accuracy","Increased initial investment"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The initial investment to develop an RPA can be very costly. Therefore, while RPA can improve efficiency, employee morale, and accuracy, those benefits must be weighed against the cost of designing and implementing the automated process.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.proc.au.001_1904","question":"Which of the following can be described by the possibility for machines to learn from experience, adjust to new inputs, and perform human-like tasks?","options":["Robotic Process Automation","Artificial Intelligence","Cloud Computing","Business Intelligence"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Artificial Intelligence relies heavily on deep learning and natural language processing. Using these technologies, computers can be trained to accomplish specific tasks by processing large amounts of data and recognizing patterns in the data.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.proc.au.002_1904","question":"Which of the following emerging technologies can help in improving the efficiency of manufacturing plant assembly operations and warehouse operations?","options":["3D printing","Robots","Virtual reality","Internet of Things"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Correct. Robotic technology or robotic process automation (RPA) improves the speed and accuracy of assembling various parts or components in a manufacturing plant, soldering and painting subassemblies and final assemblies of parts, and other labor-intensive tasks. Similarly, robots operate in a warehouse and distribution center to locate the desired product on a warehouse shelf, to place the product in a shipping container, and to get ready for shipping to a customer so the customer order is fulfilled. The overall benefits of RPA include reduced labor costs due to less time to complete tasks, increased speed and accuracy, improved worker productivity (i.e., doing more tasks in less time), reduced human errors from not shipping wrong products to customers, and increased customer satisfaction with faster and more accurate order fulfillment process.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ep.man.sys.005_1905","question":"Regarding enterprise performance management (EPM), which of the following cannot facilitate business planning and performance management functions?","options":["Workflow software","Online analytical processing technology","Spreadsheet software","Structured query language software"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Spreadsheet software cannot facilitate business planning and performance management functions. This is because the data in the spreadsheet is presented in two dimensions which cannot be updated constantly and automatically due to the limitation of the spreadsheet design principles.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.ep.man.sys.002_1906","question":"A major common element between a corporate performance management (CPM) program and a country's gross domestic product (GDP) is best reflected in which of the following performance measures?","options":["Performance","Productivity","Effectiveness","Efficiency"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A corporate performance management (CPM) program deals with productivity, effectiveness, efficiency, cycle times, and business velocities. Productivity is a company's output of goods and services divided by its inputs. This means productivity can be improved by either increasing the amount of output using the same level of inputs or reducing the number of inputs required to produce the output. Gross domestic product (GDP) measures the total market value of all final goods and services produced by a country in a given year. GDP represents the total output of a country (i.e., productivity). Hence, productivity is a common element between the CPM and GDP.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.ep.man.sys.004_1906","question":"The ultimate goal of enterprise performance management (EPM) is which of the following?","options":["Hindsight","Insight","Foresight","Visible sight"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Foresight means future showing compliance awareness, strategic planning, and operations planning. This is the ultimate goal of EPM.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ep.man.sys.004_1905","question":"Regarding the business planning and performance management aspect of enterprise performance management (EPM), which of the following is required to transform hindsight vision into foresight vision?","options":["I only","II only","III and IV","I, II, III, and IV"],"answer":"D","explanation":"All four choices are correct. Past historical results show hindsight vision. When metrics and key performance indicators are added to the hindsight vision, it gives insights. When what-if analysis and simulation models are added to the insights, it provides foresight vision. Moreover, ad hoc (on-the-fly) forecast updates can also be added to the insights to give foresight vision.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ep.man.sys.002_1905","question":"What is an EPM?","options":["Enterprise Performance Management—This process and software system are designed to help companies link their strategic goals and objectives, communicate them to management, and align them with their budgets and corporate plans.","Enterprise Payroll Management—This along with an AIS is designed to maximize job roles aligned with job performance.","Enterprise Production and Manufacturing—This system along with an ERP (Enterprise Resource Planning) enhances overall strategic goals and objectives which take into account staffing resources and job roles.","Enterprise Performance Manufacturing—This is an optimized manufacturing process that when paired with an AIS is designed to maximize productivity."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Aligning the entire company around the strategic goals and objectives is one of the main purposes of an EPM.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ep.man.sys.001_1905","question":"Corporate performance management (CPM) software is embedded in which of the following to improve performance reporting quality?","options":["One version of the analysis","One version of the truth","One version of the tools","One version of the skills"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Truth can only come in one version and there is no room for multiple versions. Multiple versions can lead to multiple interpretations, which can be confusing. Both financial data and nonfinancial data (operational data) are automatically recorded or captured in the CPM software. Later, these two types of data are reconciled to each other to achieve the goal of one version of the truth.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.ep.man.sys.003_1906","question":"Which of the following is the major benefit of implementing corporate performance management (CPM) software?","options":["Faster reporting of financial results","Continuous data collection and reporting","Automatic distribution of information to stakeholders","Reduced human intervention"],"answer":"D","explanation":"With the use of CPM software, accounting and finance staff can focus on addressing major issues than on small issues or solving day-to-day minor problems. Because the CPM software generates all the required reports automatically, no need to prepare the reports manually. Hence, no need to intervene in the functioning of the CPM software. This is a major benefit.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"aq.ep.man.sys.001_1906","question":"What is an Enterprise Performance Management (EPM) system?","options":["This is a system that optimizes overall employee satisfaction scores across the enterprise.","In conjunction with a Database Management System (DBMS), it maintains consistent data across the centralized database.","This is a process designed to help organizations maintain their Human Resources and Personal payroll.","This process and software system are designed to help companies link their strategic goals and objectives, communicate them to management, and align them with their budgets and corporate plans."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Aligning the entire company around the strategic goals and objectives is one of the main purposes of an EPM.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0},{"id":"tb.ep.man.sys.003_1905","question":"Regarding enterprise performance management (EPM), the element check in the plan-do-check-act (PDCA) cycle focuses on which of the following in order to facilitate business planning and performance management activities?","options":["Orders and sales","Metrics and key performance indicators","Market and financial projections","Rolling forecasts"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Metrics and key performance indicators focus on the check element in the PDCA cycle.","unit":20,"subunit":"20.1","volume":"supplemental","source":"Supplemental answer-source documents","questionNumber":0}];